# passages/00010-RumorD2.mws.yaml
RumorD2_001=No matter how I attempted to engage conversation, the frilly aristocrat ignored me. What sight in this dingy statehouse could possibly provoke him into silenced awe? Flustered, I secured my overcoat and made to leave. 
RumorD2_002=However, the moment I pivoted to make my exit, the gentleman turned towards me. Without words, I was handed a small metal figure in the shape of a {figure}.
RumorD2_003="Resist." He stated with firm conviction, and then exited before me, his frilly coat flapping in the wind.
RumorD2_005=Gain the {figure} token.

# passages/00011-RumorD3.mws.yaml
RumorD3_001=The older woman smiled as I approached and after a brief introduction was very amenable to sharing her opinion.
RumorD3_002="The rumor is that the Unified Monarchists are willing to aid the townspeople with goods and services. Long live His Majesty."
RumorD3_003=I was able to interpret her further meanderings to mean that **any player who supports the Unified Monarchists receives a Resource of their choice.**
RumorD3_004=She continued, "And if these unconcerned military types ever ask for your assistance in **quartering** troops, just say yes. They will force you to do so anyway."

# passages/00012-RumorD4.mws.yaml
RumorD4_001="Down with the Monarchy!" the group shouts in unison. 
RumorD4_002=My intrusion was met with jeers and skepticism until I allayed their worries with a clever turn of phrase and charming demeanor.
RumorD4_003=I was quick to explain to them the merits of dour discretion when royal matters are concerned.
RumorD4_004=They became especially excited by my presence - commonfolk are so easily distracted - and
RumorD4_005=After a moment of stunned silence - clearly they were overtaken by my brilliance -
RumorD4_006={_rnd_RumorD4_0} {_rnd_RumorD4_1} a young woman pulled me aside and explained the oppressive politics of the current regime at length.
RumorD4_007=I was able to discern one very important piece of information: **Any player who supports the Separatists gains 2VP.**

# passages/00013-RumorD5.mws.yaml
RumorD5_001=The snaggle-toothed gentleman waved me closer as I approached. When I was within a few paces, he rushed to me and knelt, holding both of my hands in his. My eyes watered at his reproachable stench.
RumorD5_002="Repent, young fisher," He said. "The end is near. The battle is lost. Lost. Lost. Lost." He shivered as his unkempt beard shook with white dust.
RumorD5_003=I felt it may have been a mistake to speak to this unfortunate soul and quickly made my leave. I was annoyed to later discover that the man had deftly placed a misshapen wooden carving in my shoulderbag.
RumorD5_004=Gain a {icon:s3_woodenfiguretoken} token.
RumorD5_005=The snaggle-toothed gentleman sniffed the air as I came near - though his odorous presence could be felt from across the room. This action was followed by a long, awkward silence, during which he did not break eye contact with me.
RumorD5_006=Suddenly, he reached into his torn pocket and pulled out a misshapen wooden figure. He leaned in close and whispered in my ear, his breath like fermented trout. "We will be safe. John will keep you safe. The war will never touch us. I promise, Captain."

# passages/00014-TowardsWar.mws.yaml
TowardsWar_001=A Town Fully Defended
TowardsWar_003=Remove all player pieces from the board and perform the End of the Generation. Return any unused {icon:s3_sickletoken} , {icon:s3_shieldtoken} , and {icon:s3_woodenfiguretoken} tokens to the Scenario box.
TowardsWar_004=The {warwinner} have pushed the battlefront away from our fair village and taken command of the local government. 
TowardsWar_005=Against my wishes, the Barracks was built by the {warwinner}, further strengthening their position in the region. It seems that my progeny will need to be more forceful in the direction of this conflict.
TowardsWar_006=True to our instructions, the **Barracks** was built by the {warwinner}, further strengthening their position in the region. Although, I will not see the end of this conflict in my lifetime, due to my efforts, this esteemed and instrumental legacy will continue.
TowardsWar_007=It is fitting that I came mewling into this cold world, struggling each day against the ignorance of men, and now I make my exit amidst this turmoil. For it is only through struggle and remorseless ambition that one can claw their way into the annals of history!

# passages/00015-TakeEvent.mws.yaml
TakeEvent_003=On a brisk April morning, my family was called upon to attend another Town Hall meeting. This time, however, the atmosphere was especially heated.
TakeEvent_004=Being conscious of the dominant attitudes in town, I understood that the prevailing preference was for the {warwinner} forces. As influential members of the aristocratic establishment, it was inevitable that the military officers turned to us for support in building a barracks within the village. Oh what a frivolous distraction matters of politics prove to be!
TakeEvent_005=**Vote**
TakeEvent_006=Each player takes a {warwinner} and {warloser} token into their fist and secretly chooses a side. When all players have chosen, simultaneously reveal your votes.
TakeEvent_007=**{warwinner}**: Is a vote to build the Barracks.
TakeEvent_008=**{warloser}**: Is a vote against.
TakeEvent_009=Tally the vote count (ties are broken by the player who went last during the Middle Years).
TakeEvent_010=Click to begin the vote...

# passages/00016-TimeTravelintro.mws.yaml
TimeTravelintro_001=A Town in Shambles
TimeTravelintro_002=Words failed to capture the scope of my sorrow. War, in all its awful beauty had befallen the once handsome province.
TimeTravelintro_003=May my eyes never gaze upon another site so desolate and horrible as the scorched landscape left in ruin by the indifference of conflict. My blood ran cold, as if buried in this tainted, upturned soil. It felt as if my heart - like the rusted hinge of a coffin - had swung shut, steeling itself from the bleak, harsh world around me.
TimeTravelintro_004=Turn to page **12** in the Village Chronicle.

