# passages/00020-TimeEnd2.mws.yaml
TimeEnd2_001=Fully Repaired
TimeEnd2_002=**Rusty, But Worth a Try**Forced to confront the spectre of mortality in my final years, I knew that without swift, decisive action, I might never have the opportunity to see the results of my journey through time.
TimeEnd2_003=I, for one, was ready to busk it. Though the machine that bore us was left incomplete, perhaps it was stout enough to risk a second voyage.
TimeEnd2_004=**How many of the** _Time Machine Repairs_ **Experiments have you repaired in total?**
TimeEnd2_005=Zero.
TimeEnd2_007=One.
TimeEnd2_008=one piece
TimeEnd2_009=Two.
TimeEnd2_010=two pieces
TimeEnd2_011=I knew that I had completed the infernal **Time Machine** to the utmost of my ability, meticulously inspecting each individual part, many of which were far more advanced than anything the world had thus far envisioned.
TimeEnd2_012=Though my years have advanced and my vigor has left me, it is my hope that this final act will ensure the lustrous future which war had wrenched from me so long ago. Once more I venture into this box so my eyes will witness what I have wrought. Whether it is my coffin or my ship to sail amongst the cosmos, I welcome what fate lies in store for me.

# passages/00021-ResolutionofEvent.mws.yaml
ResolutionofEvent_001=The Town's Reaction
ResolutionofEvent_002=For reasons which I cannot fathom, our collective referendum was received with mild acceptance. While it stifled the construction temporarily, the town's allegiance remained unwavering.
ResolutionofEvent_003=Could it be that I had underestimated the scope of their ignorance? How was it that even under pressure from {playtxt} aristocratic financiers they remained apprehensive and defiant?
ResolutionofEvent_004=I was quite convinced that strengthening our relationship with the dominant faction and encouraging a route towards inevitable conflict would ensure a fresh demand for my experiments. If that sentiment aligned with the bedraggled populace, then so be it.
ResolutionofEvent_005=All players who voted to build the Barracks receive a Flag token and flip it {warwinner} side up
ResolutionofEvent_006= and **gain 2VP**
ResolutionofEvent_007= and **gain 2 Resources of their choice**
ResolutionofEvent_008=All players who voted against building the Barracks receive a Flag token and flip it {warloser} side up

# passages/00022-AMessenger.mws.yaml
AMessenger_001=A Messenger Arrives
AMessenger_003=On a Saturday afternoon, I was hustled to the entryway by my caretaker. A young messenger was nervously tapping her leather boots against the stone. In her left hand was a small figurine in the shape of a {crest}, which I had left by the windowsill. Her eyes were scanning the room and she was visibly startled by our speedy return. The caretaker muttered his apologies, calling her a thief, but I calmed his nerves quickly.
AMessenger_004=**The messenger turned and spoke to the player with the {crest} token.**

