# passages/00025-Amessyes.mws.yaml
Amessyes_001=**Carefully hand this Storybook device to the player with the {crest} token and do not allow any other players to see the screen.**
Amessyes_002=The Messenger reached into her shoulderbag and retrieved a letter, which she handed to me. When I hesitated, she nodded, apparently unable to leave until I had provided an answer.
Amessyes_003=Inside the envelope was a formal letter of thanks from a {warwinner} military official. My parents had noted a keen interest in a possible business venture during wartime. The letter contained blueprints for an addition to my estate, which would be used to house goods seized from members of the resistance forces and sympathizers.

# passages/00026-Amessno.mws.yaml
Amessno_001=No Importance
Amessno_002=What a rude and frankly, under-dressed fellow for visiting with the aristocracy. The messenger sped to the gate upon hearing my reply. 
Amessno_003=I only note this situation to remind others of the vagrantry within the Austro-Hungarian empire these days. Seems these bedraggled couriers are trying to play us for a fool, expecting our allegiances to pay dividends for their unsavory habits. If we ever needed science to find a cure for beggars, there would be no time like the present.
Amessno_004=Nothing happens. Discard the {crest} token to the scenario box.

