# passages/00028-ParadoxIntro.mws.yaml
ParadoxIntro_001=You Cant Stop Progress
ParadoxIntro_003=**A Brighter Future**
ParadoxIntro_005=I remember being stunned as I arrived by train on a mid-summer's evening. I do not know what I expected from the anecdotes my nanny had relayed to me, but it was not the bustling cityscape that greeted me. As the sun dipped into the forest, the glimmer of modern steel light fixtures amplified the urban luminescence. My delighted spouse and I enjoyed a quiet ride in our steamer car, which offered us a chance to observe the idyllic community and decidedly pleasant folk enjoying the convenience of electricity and steam turbine technology.
ParadoxIntro_007=When I spoke of my family's history of experimentation, I was rarely met with indifference but more often firm words of encouragement. It appeared that this region, so rife with abnormal progress, viewed my theories as rudimentary but delightfully avant-garde. Even when I expounded upon dark rituals and the grotesque, they encouraged further exploration and referred me to the newly constructed University.

# passages/00029-Paradox1.mws.yaml
Paradox1_002=Turn to page **15** of the Village Chronicle.

# passages/00030-AMessno2.mws.yaml
AMessno2_002=It was a brief correspondence from an acquaintance of mine from university. While the contents did not intrigue me, the lack of political speak was refreshing and spurred me to contemplation. For the next few days, I was overcome with the creative impulse that security and seclusion provided.
AMessno2_003=**Draw an Experiment card from the deck of your choice.** Then, discard the {figure} token to the scenario box.

# passages/00031-TimeTravelIntro2.mws.yaml
TimeTravelIntro2_001=A Well Timed Discovery
TimeTravelIntro2_002=If you disbelieve the next portion of my story, I would think you of sound mind to do so. I will withhold the specific details of the location, but the cryptic map led us to an abandoned silver mine near the ruined village. With lanterns held high, my cousins and I crept forward into the darkened mineshaft, following the curve of iron tracks to an alcove where warning signs had been posted by the last workers years ago.
TimeTravelIntro2_003=As we approached, a metal box began to hum. Blue sparks crackled from the edges of the box, fully illuminating the cave. With a sudden flash, a door on the metal device swung open and thick fog cascaded along the rails. Coincidentally, {playtxt} leather seats were situated against the interior walls of the machine. 
TimeTravelIntro2_004=Without a moment's deliberation, we ambled through the entrance and buckled ourselves in. As we each tightened the buckles about us, we heard a loud hissing sound like the escaping of steam through unseen vents, and the door slammed shut. The metallic walls shook violently, jolting us against our constraints.
TimeTravelIntro2_005=A set of dials spun individually, settling on the number **1831** while reality folded like a silk curtain around us.
TimeTravelIntro2_006=Click to travel through time and space...

