# passages/00040-ResistEnd.mws.yaml
ResistEnd_001=Victory for the Resistance
ResistEnd_002=Resistance Quashed
ResistEnd_003=With **so few buildings destroyed**, the message was clear that the resistance was weak. My final years confirmed a return to normalcy as the efforts of the resisting faction within the region were suppressed and the {warwinner} remained vigilant and victorious.
ResistEnd_004=It was just as I had planned. What a tragedy that mortality dims our eyes just as the dawn's light crests the hills of innovation. I only wish that the next generation knew how I suffered to ensure their triumph.
ResistEnd_007=With **{wardestroy} buildings destroyed**, the message was clear that they were not wanted. Driven by the will of the people and undoubtedly terrified by the enormity of my scientific contributions, the bloodied and beaten faction that had controlled the town limped into the distance leaving the {warloser} to celebrate their victory.

# passages/00041-MonarchReignIntro.mws.yaml
MonarchReignIntro_001=Heavy is the Crown
MonarchReignIntro_002=Influence is gained in two ways: through money (that alluring and insidious scratch) and through bloodshed. Though my years on this foul Earth are few, in this abbreviated time I have learned this one valuable truth.
MonarchReignIntro_003=The voracious objections of the townsfolk had become so commonplace that to see them reduced to sneering murmurs was a marked improvement that made my excursions to the village supremely more tolerable. The Separatist movement had dissipated with time, which put an end to this exasperating (yet lucrative) warring business and the peasantry returned to their normal state of impotent discontent.
MonarchReignIntro_004=By this time, our family's influence had bent the ear of the throne. With keen use of investment capital, we were afforded an advisory position that could be employed to sway official opinion and deal with regional matters. This presented a delicate balance: As long as our work went unnoticed, we could avoid all consequences and remain influential. Once noticed, however, we could never return to the same peace once afforded. Heavy is the head that wears the crown, as the bard says.
MonarchReignIntro_005=I was excited at the proposition, and instructed my servants to be at their finest for potential visitors; because while I grew lethargic at the thought of entertaining clerical matters of the crown, I fully recognized the power that one could wield with proper control of the state. And whether I had to bury them in gold or watch the rivers run red with blood, I would be afforded that power!

# passages/00042-PeaceIntro.mws.yaml
PeaceIntro_001=Peace Through War
PeaceIntro_002=I arrived just in time for the festivities. The normally dour gothic architecture was festooned with brightly colored ribbons, balloons, and pots overflowing with borscht. The conquering soldiers paraded down the cobblestone streets in formation and uniform, ticker tape celebrating the Separatists’ victory. Such a remarkable contrast between the slipshod militias of my youth and the democratic revolutionaries cheering the Hungarian name in time with each stomp of a soldier's boot.
PeaceIntro_003=However, it was not this boring pageantry that ignited an infernal passion within me, it was the passion of the people. Emboldened by their conquest of a royal power and enlivened with pride in their country, this righteous fervor became a frenzy. Within weeks, an extreme nationalist party began to take hold and this brief respite from war was suddenly punctuated by lofty ambitions. 
PeaceIntro_004=The government had realized that the only way to ensure a lasting peace in the country and the tumultuous surrounding territories was to properly exercise military force to coerce cooperation. My family's reputation within the scientific community had positioned me as the foremost authority in experimental weaponry. I relished the opportunity to observe the devastative effects of these marvelous machinations by attempting to take over the world.
PeaceIntro_005=With my technological arsenal leading the charge, no nation could hope to resist our power! Our army would ensure a lasting peace that would enshrine my legacy forever in the annals of human history. There was not a moment to waste! It was time to change the world with science!

# passages/00043-MonarchReign1.mws.yaml
MonarchReign1_002=Turn to page **9** of the Village Chronicle.
MonarchReign1_010=The player who makes the most decrees will gain a **bonus** at the End of the Generation.
MonarchReign1_017=Any player with a {icon:creepy_icon} Marker on their Score Track Marker, **loses 1VP** any time they would gain {icon:creepy_icon}.

# passages/00044-Peace1.mws.yaml
Peace1_002=Turn to page **11** of the Village Chronicle. 
Peace1_008=The Empire has decided to expand by utilizing the implements of destruction which you have provided. You may draw a card from the Advanced Weaponry deck when taking any action that allows you to draw Experiments. When you complete the Experiment, you will receive {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens equal to the amount listed at the bottom of the card.
Peace1_010=Click here at the end of the Round...

# passages/00045-Peace2.mws.yaml
Peace2_005=Click here at the end of the round...

# passages/00046-Peace3.mws.yaml
Peace3_001=**Office of Public Relations**
Peace3_002=At the End of the Generation, after the Final Battle, the player(s) with the most remaining **Weapon** tokens gains a Vanity Estate Upgrade of their choice.
Peace3_003={icon:storybooktoken} **Final Conflict**
