Peace3_005=Click here at the End of the Generation for the Final Battle...

# passages/00047-PeaceEvent.mws.yaml
PeaceEvent_001=Loyalty by Force or Diplomacy
PeaceEvent_002=My ingenious creations had successfully turned the tide of the World War in our favor. With the entirety of the Eastern European front coalescing to our demands and the remainder of the continent on the verge of surrender, it was clear that no force on the planet was stronger than our nation.
PeaceEvent_003=However, the consistent uprisings and insurgent activities among the populace was diverting our precious resources. The generals feared that without loyal public support an insurrection could topple all of our designs from the inside. 
PeaceEvent_004=It was suggested that we should embark on an aggressive propaganda campaign that promoted our values of freedom and national pride to motivate the people. Alternatively, modern advancements in chemistry were astonishing. It would be a simple matter to make an example of a single city by strategically releasing a mustard gas concoction. An inexpensive and very effective solution.

# passages/00048-TimeTravelEvent.mws.yaml
TimeTravelEvent_001=Advanced Work is Important!
TimeTravelEvent_002=While the journal was an astonishing discovery in itself, I did not realize that the true revelation would arrive several weeks later while I sampled brandy upon my veranda. A swirl of stormclouds suddenly converged overhead, and with a spear of electricity a fantastic metal contraption appeared. The {playtxt} travelers emerged, wrinkles lining their features and gray, wispy hair held back by jeweler's goggles strapped to their heads. 
TimeTravelEvent_003=Our meeting was brief, but over a brunch of polenta and egg-plant stuffed with forcemeat, they relinquished control of several new schematics which they claimed had been retrieved from the future and would revolutionize the modern world. As one may have surmised from this encounter, the intrepid traveler was none other than my long-lost parent, here to entrust one final piece of my legacy.
TimeTravelEvent_004=With these experiments, they implored, I could work towards a true Utopia - a world of technological perfection. 
TimeTravelEvent_005=Return the **Time Machine Repair** cards to the Scenario box.
TimeTravelEvent_006=Retrieve the **Utopian Experiments** from the Scenario box. Shuffle them face-down and place them nearby to form a deck. 

# passages/00049-BlameGameEvent.mws.yaml
BlameGameEvent_001=Paradoxical Dilemma
BlameGameEvent_002=But this was inadequate! Was I to gamble the life's work of not one but two generations on a single vote? If this war continued, all that we had created would be lost! How could my cousins not realize the tenuous position thrust upon us? To experiment and perish or to spend my days ignoring that which I most desired; the choice was unbearable!
BlameGameEvent_003=I felt that we needed a more decisive solution and I expressed several plans, which were unceremoniously dismissed by my simple-minded cousins. 
BlameGameEvent_004=But it was when I was bedridden, at my lowest point, sick with despair, that a knock on my door roused me from my convalescence. Little did I realize that the answer to our quandary would arrive right at my doorstep.

# passages/00050-WarningIntro.mws.yaml
WarningIntro_001=Future Consequences
WarningIntro_002=**A Modern Future**
WarningIntro_003=I remember being stunned as I arrived by train on a mid-summer's evening. I do not know what I expected from the anecdotes my nanny had relayed to me, but it was not the bustling cityscape that greeted me. As the sun dipped into the forest, the glimmer of modern steel light fixtures amplified the urban luminescence. My delighted spouse and I enjoyed a quiet ride in our steamer car which offered us a chance to observe the idyllic community and decidedly pleasant folk enjoying the convenience of electricity and steam turbine technology.
WarningIntro_004=However, when I spoke of my family's history of experimentation, I was rarely met with indifference but more often firm words of encouragement. It appeared that this region, so rife with abnormal progress, viewed my theories as rudimentary but delightfully avant-garde. Even when I expounded upon dark rituals and the grotesque, they encouraged further exploration and referred me to the newly constructed University.

# passages/00051-TimeEnd3.mws.yaml
TimeEnd3_001=Remove all player pieces from the board and Perform the End of a Generation. Return your Masterwork face-up once again. Any {icon:s3_paradoxtoken} tokens remaining on your Experiments are place into your Quarters.
TimeEnd3_002=DEAD CODE MAYBE USEFUL
TimeEnd3_003=**Early Advancement**
TimeEnd3_004=The town was inspired by my industrious attitude, whether or not that industrious nature made shivers run down the small of their back. 
TimeEnd3_005=Count the number of total **Utopian Experiments** completed:
TimeEnd3_006=If the number is **{per}** or more, 
TimeEnd3_007=If the number is fewer than **{per}**, 

# passages/00052-Warning1.mws.yaml
Warning1_001=Peaceful Return

# passages/00053-WarningEvent.mws.yaml
WarningEvent_001=The Time Travelers Appear
WarningEvent_002=In a brief instant, the trajectory of the universe shifted. I am not sure if anyone will ever read these words, as even now they flutter in and out of existence on the page.
WarningEvent_003=While enjoying a friendly sitting room conversation in the company of my cousins, our teacups were rattled by some unknown force. With a blinding flash, a curious, metal, box-like device appeared before us, sparks and embers swirling in the resultant wall of dust.
WarningEvent_004=Suddenly, the door burst open and the body of a reptilian beast sliced through the fog; its eyes a glossy white. It fell to the singed carpet, lifeless, it's neck sliced open yet cauterized, though a fresh burst of dark blood pooled onto the stone beneath it. Could it be? A dinosaur?
WarningEvent_005=A white-haired woman emerged from the chemical mist, clutching her side. The elderly lady was dressed in metallic attire that was both intriguing and exotic. The shiny material was frayed as though some impossibly large claws had shredded it, while splatters of liquid (much of it dark red) adorned her outfit. Behind her, 
WarningEvent_006=another scientist
WarningEvent_007=two other scientists
WarningEvent_008=three other scientists
WarningEvent_009=four other scientists
WarningEvent_010= sat, tethered to their seats by firm belts.
WarningEvent_011=Strained words issued from her lips: "Thank god I've found you! You must close the time loop. Oh, how brash we were! To assume we could tamper with fourth-dimensional forces! Our miscalculation will now be your doom. Soon, time as we know it will cease to exist." She beckoned to us, but her gaunt features paled when the room was suddenly cast in a crimson glow.
WarningEvent_012="I am too late! It's already happening!" she screamed, before the world reformed itself around her.

# passages/00054-TimeWarp.mws.yaml
TimeWarp_002=I could see a rift - a shimmering slice in the fabric of time -  open up before me.
TimeWarp_003=After conducting my business, I felt the Earth tremble beneath my feet. My blood vessels pulsed, bulging varicose above my straining muscles as an unseen force seemed to press upon me.
TimeWarp_004=A bolt of lightning carved through the pathway ahead, sending my carriage to an abrupt halt. The air swirled into a violent tornado around me.
TimeWarp_005=My stomach fell. A lump caught in my throat.
TimeWarp_007=**Lost in Time** - All player pieces are removed from the Town board and placed in Lost.
TimeWarp_008=The player who took the action that triggered this Time Shift **gains {_rnd_TimeWarp_0}VP**.

# passages/00056-Warning2.mws.yaml
Warning2_002=Turn to page **{cont}** of the Village Chronicle. 
Warning2_015=There was an eerily serene quality to this world. The air was dense here, like a warm blanket against the skin yet still room temperature. Green grass framed the clean roads and idyllic town setting where newspapers printed the news of the day - "Nothing to Report. Peace and Prosperity Continue." Something about it was so comforting and surreal that it was difficult to keep my eyes open. I wondered if this was what contentment feels like?
Warning2_017=We felt a deep lethargy overtake us anytime we attempted experimentation in such a perfect environment. You must assign **2** legal pieces in order to take the **Perform Experiment** action.
Warning2_030=Suddenly, a thunderous noise erupted, reverberating against the stone walls. In the distance, we watched as towering beasts of the Mesozoic Era roamed across the dusty plains. The tyrannosaurus stalked its prey, its face glimmering brightly like a bronze statue. Moments later, a bright laser burst from its eye-socket, singling out a lone brachiosaurus from the herd and cutting it in twain. As the biomechanical menace masticated it's freshly charred meal, we determined that this may be a rather difficult environment in which to continue our experiments.
Warning2_034=When the the round is complete, 
Warning2_035=click here to move to the next round...

# passages/00057-WarningEvent2.mws.yaml
WarningEvent2_001=A Semblance of Stasis
WarningEvent2_002=The sky no longer glows crimson as we arrive in this timeline. Is it possible that we have returned to our original timeline, or close enough given the intricacies of time travel?
WarningEvent2_003=However, with the fabric of time rehealing itself, we realized that only a constant in our generational ambitions would solidify the timeline:
WarningEvent2_004=**We must finish our Great-Grandfather's Masterwork!**

# passages/00058-Warning2time.mws.yaml
Warning2time_002=When a player completes a Masterwork this Generation, 

# passages/00059-Warning3.mws.yaml
Warning3_001=Turn to page **{cont}** of the Village Chronicle
Warning3_002=There was an eerily serene quality to this world. The air was dense there, like a warm blanket against the skin yet still room temperature. Green grass framed the clean roads and idyllic town setting where newspapers printed the news of the day - "Nothing to Report. Peace and Prosperity Continue." Something about it was so comforting and surreal that it was difficult to keep my eyes open. I wondered if this was what contentment feels like?
Warning3_003=We feel a deep lethargy overtake us any time we attempt experimentation in such a perfect environment. You must assign **2** legal pieces in order to take the **Perform Experiment** action.
Warning3_004=Suddenly, a thunderous noise erupted, reverberating against the stone walls. In the distance, we watched as towering beasts of the Mesozoic Era roamed across the dusty plains. The tyrannosaurus stalked its prey, its face glimmering brightly like a bronze statue. Moments later, a bright laser burst from its eye-socket, singling out a lone brachiosaurus from the herd and cutting it in twain. 
Warning3_005=As the biomechanical menace masticated it's freshly charred meal, we determined that this may be a rather difficult environment in which to continue our experiments.

