# passages/00061-Stasis.mws.yaml
Stasis_001=Timeline Stabilized
Stasis_002=I felt the fiber of my being congeal from an oscillating tension I had endured for so long that my blood could no longer perceive it. The sky remained red for a brief moment, a faint electronic chord sounded, and neon grid-like lines flashed through all the objects in the world before disappearing once again. The time-loop had been closed.
Stasis_003=As expected, as soon as the deed was completed, the original time traveling {playtxt} returned once again; or in this case, for the first time. They seemed oblivious to what had transpired in the past or how my cousins and I viewed them as the cause of decades of suffering and interruption.
Stasis_004=Elderly as they were, they were easily dispatched. 
Stasis_005=I messaged my cousins, declaring that the time machine was secured. They seemed grateful that peace had finally been restored and nothing more would interrupt our important work.
Stasis_006=The player who completed their Masterwork **gains 5VP**.
Stasis_007=Each player **gains 1** {icon:bodies_icon}.

# passages/00062-TimeTravelintro1.mws.yaml
TimeTravelintro1_001=A Return to Devastation
TimeTravelintro1_003=I hope you will indulge my brief melancholic digression, for even my stern disposition was reduced to sobbing when I discovered the grim remnants of what was once a burgeoning village. I knew of the tragedy, having received several letters urging me to delay my visit until the conflict had been resolved. However, I felt compelled to see the destruction with my own eyes, and even braved the last vestiges of war to do so. If only I had taken heed of their warning...
TimeTravelintro1_004=The all-encompassing destruction had blackened the fields, leaving the land ashen and emaciated. The once-grand estate was now in shambles; a dilapidated husk of its former intimidating presence. I wept for what seemed like hours amongst the dust and rubble. While I was still heir to a considerable fortune with diverse business interests, I was struck by the sentimental weight of such a loss.
TimeTravelintro1_005=However, fortune would soon shine its myriad gaze upon me.
TimeTravelintro1_006=I was joined by my cousins and we shared our grief at a hotel in Budapest for several days. It was there that an unexpected messenger arrived with a small brown package. Inside, the executor of our parents’ affairs had included the remaining articles of interest salvaged from the mansion. As if preserved for this moment, there was a leather journal seemingly untouched by the flames. Upon opening the tome, a weathered sheet of parchment fell to the table. 
TimeTravelintro1_007=It was a map!

# passages/00064-Blame1b.mws.yaml
Blame1b_001=Offer
Blame1b_003=The riflemen conferred for a moment, their mustaches quivering with their whispers. One of the soldiers then smiled congenially.
Blame1b_004="We are always looking for generous benefactors. For a sum of **$2**, we will kindly sell you a new flag. A flag of the proud {warwinner}. And we will be willing to overlook this error in judgement."
Blame1b_005=Do you accept the offer of **$2** to purchase a {warwinner} Flag token?
Blame1b_006=Yes, I accept.
Blame1b_007=Sorry. I must sadly decline.

# passages/00065-Blame1c.mws.yaml
Blame1c_001=Passing the Blame
Blame1c_002=The soldiers took a moment to inform me of the true reason for their untimely intrusion. The townsfolk had heard of some strange occurrences in the hills surrounding the valley, and whispers of traitorous activities had the {warwinner} forces suspicious. They asked me if I had any information on the subject.
Blame1c_003=I was struck by a **sudden epiphany!**
Blame1c_004=If my cousins and I could vote one of us as a target of their ire, perhaps this would further sway history and avoid the destruction of the estate in the coming years.
Blame1c_005=I knew that whoever was chosen would suffer - and **immediately discard 1 Estate Upgrade from their Estate and gain 2** {icon:creepy_icon}**.** We'd be punished if there wasn't a clear winner. But, what was one life sacrificed to rectify the entirety of all history?
Blame1c_006=I decided:
Blame1c_007=To stay silent.
Blame1c_008=To blame {nameB}.
Blame1c_009=To blame {nameC}.
Blame1c_010=To blame {nameD}.
Blame1c_011=To blame {nameE}.
Blame1c_012=To blame {nameA}.

