# passages/00070-MartialSepEvent.mws.yaml
MartialSepEvent_001=Escalation
MartialSepEvent_002=As the war pressed on relentlessly, it was I who suffered most terribly. With embattlements requiring constant provisions, procuring the necessary ingredients for my experiments became increasingly more difficult. 
MartialSepEvent_003=However, in my humble brilliance I settled on a firm solution based upon one simple question: Why do I need specialty ingredients when I can just attach guns to everything? 
MartialSepEvent_004=Certainly this slapdash methodology was not ideal nor dignified, but it certainly achieved a devastative result. Why my first practical demonstration caused both sides to cease hostilities after witnessing a small battalion reduced to a mere wine stain upon the battlefield.
MartialSepEvent_005=However, the regional military factions required additional convincing as the use of our weapons was still considered a "war crime" and would require further convincing to employ these additional methods. Imagine, "science" being considered a war crime? Is it not a general's hope to reach an efficient victory? 

# passages/00071-HowtoWar.mws.yaml
HowtoWar_001=Deploying Advanced Weaponry
HowtoWar_002=At the end of each round, players will use their {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens to bid on two battlefields that increase in value. 
HowtoWar_003=At the end of each round, players will use their {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens to bid on three battlefields that increase in value. 
HowtoWar_004=The first Battle of each round is worth 2VP and the second is worth 3VP.
HowtoWar_005=The first Battle of each round is worth 3VP and the second is worth 5VP.
HowtoWar_006=The first Battle of each round is worth 2VP, the second is worth 3VP, and the third is worth 5VP.
HowtoWar_007= During the Late Years, the Final Battles will be worth double the VP.
HowtoWar_010=The player(s) who revealed the most tokens receives the VP listed. If more than one player revealed the same amount, all players that revealed the most tokens receive all points. 
HowtoWar_011=For the Final Battle, the Battle card will be turned to the opposite **Final Battle** side. For this battle, **each territory is worth additional points.** 
HowtoWar_012=_ALL revealed tokens are placed into the supply, no matter the outcome._ 

# passages/00072-BattleTime.mws.yaml
BattleTime_001=Glory and Recognition
BattleTime_002=I alone deserved recognition for my glorious, bombastic, chimerical, transformative creations that defied the rigors of known science. I could no longer suffer the egotistical competitive nature of my cousins, whose work so paled in comparison to my own. This was my time. This was the era of {_rnd_BattleTime_0} III!
BattleTime_003=The fate of the world rested in my hands. It was my discoveries, my ingenious weaponry, my unslakable ambitions that would define this new epoch in human existence. And I put on a demonstration that left no doubt as to whom the glory should be bestowed upon.
BattleTime_004=Fame meant little to me if it did not carry with it the power to alter the world. I would watch as it transformed - carefully molded by my own hands - into a boundless utopia. My influence could no longer be relegated to the shadows. It was time to claim the Earth for my own and shake it to its very core.
BattleTime_005=All players take all their {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens into their hands. For each battle, starting with the upper-most territory (marked by the Occult cube), the players secretly decide how many tokens to place into their right hand and extend their fist to the center of the table. Once all players have decided, all players reveal their tokens.
BattleTime_006=The player(s) who revealed the most tokens receives the VP listed. If more than one player revealed the same amount, all players that revealed the most tokens receive all points. _ALL revealed tokens are placed into the supply, no matter the outcome._
BattleTime_007=Click to begin the battle...

# passages/00073-Paradox2.mws.yaml
Paradox2_005= at the end of the Generation will gain this tile at no cost. _If there is a tie, the one with the fewest VP receives the tile._

# passages/00074-ParadoxEvent.mws.yaml
ParadoxEvent_001=Monument to Progress
ParadoxEvent_002=Rebuilding
ParadoxEvent_003=The town offered a token of their appreciation for setting their trajectory towards a Utopian future.
ParadoxEvent_004=The player with the most completed Utopian Experiments **gains the In Memoriam** Estate Upgrade.
ParadoxEvent_005=The player who has moved the furthest along the {icon:insanity_icon} Track **gains the In Memoriam** Estate Upgrade.
ParadoxEvent_006= _If there is a tie, the one with the fewest VP receives the tile. If still tied, the tile is discarded._ This upgrade can be placed into a new slot at no expansion cost.
ParadoxEvent_007=With no monument built, the remaining people in the region set to the unfortunate task of reconstructing a landscape torn apart by time paradoxes and interdimensional beings.
ParadoxEvent_008=It was a bitter pill to swallow. I had done so much; given so much of myself. To receive no reward for offering the gift of time travel to the world - despite the total and utter chaos it affected - tainted my otherwise impeccable reputation.

# passages/00076-FinalBattleTime.mws.yaml
FinalBattleTime_001=FINAL BATTLE
FinalBattleTime_002=Despite our superior weapon technology and a pioneering reinterpretation of ethics in conflict, some of the neighboring countries still refused to be subjugated. The generals were prepared for a final push which would determine the outcome of the conflict and if this glorious empire would reign above all else.
FinalBattleTime_003=**Battle Reminder**
FinalBattleTime_004=The player(s) who revealed the most tokens receives the VP listed. If more than one player played the same amount, all players that revealed the most tokens receive all points. _ALL revealed tokens are placed into the supply, no matter the outcome._
FinalBattleTime_005=Turn the Battle card to the opposite **Final Battle** side. For this battle, **each territory is worth additional points.**
FinalBattleTime_006=The Battle card remains with the current side up _(and is NOT turned to the Final Battle side.)_

# passages/00077-StoryBook.mws.yaml
StoryBook_001=How to Use the Storybook
StoryBook_002=My Father's Work is a game of Victorian era mad scientist ambition told over three generations. The Storybook App controls the direction of the Town depending on the decisions made by players. It will require that players interact with it by clicking on specific passages at certain times.
StoryBook_003=**End of Round**
StoryBook_004=There are 3 rounds in each Generation. At the end of each round, you **must** click the bottom link to resolve any special events and move play to the next round. The screen will then display the current round, and changes to gameplay (if any).
StoryBook_005=**Story Actions**
StoryBook_006=Sometimes the game will require that a player click a certain link when an action has been performed. This may be taking an action in the Town, your Estate, or completing a specific goal. Be sure to click these links to receive a special story passage.

# passages/00079-BlameOut1.mws.yaml
BlameOut1_001=Diverting Their Attentions
BlameOut1_002=In an attempt to pacify the local military, my cousins and I mutually agreed to assign blame for their enemies' intelligence onto one of our own.
BlameOut1_003=**{blame}** arrived home from a weekend sojourn to discover that their Estate had been ransacked by the soldiers. In a barbaric display against disloyalty, a portion of the domain had been set ablaze. Fortunately, the caretaker and servants were able to stave off the fire before it consumed the entirety of the lot.
BlameOut1_004=**{blame} must immediately discard one Estate Upgrade from their Estate and gains 2** {icon:creepy_icon}**.** _If they do not have an Estate Upgrade built, they must instead lose 5VP._

# passages/00080-BlameOut2.mws.yaml
BlameOut2_001=Crossed Signals
BlameOut2_002=While several of us pointed fingers at one another in a display of petty competitiveness, the soldiers were unable to discern a traitor **with more votes than the others** from amongst our ranks. They were notably displeased with our bickering and the wasted time they invested into inquiries around the villa.
BlameOut2_003=In a blunt exertion of power, the soldiers excised a tax from myself and all of my cousins, which we were obliged to pay under threat of bodily injury. I pledged my distinguished service in scientific pursuits to their cause, which they vehemently (and rudely) declined.
BlameOut2_004={nameA} remained silent and **discards 1 Resource** of any type from their Estate or **returns a Servant to Lost**.
BlameOut2_005={nameB} remained silent and **discards 1 Resource** of any type from their Estate or **returns a Servant to Lost**.
BlameOut2_006={nameC} remained silent and **discards 1 Resource** of any type from their Estate or **returns a Servant to Lost**.
BlameOut2_007={nameD} remained silent and **discards 1 Resource** of any type from their Estate or **returns a Servant to Lost**.
BlameOut2_008={nameE} remained silent and **discards 1 Resource** of any type from their Estate or **returns a Servant to Lost**.
BlameOut2_009=All other players must **discard 2 Resources** of any type from their Estate or **return a Servant to Lost**.

# passages/00081-BlameOut3.mws.yaml
BlameOut3_001=Silence is Golden
BlameOut3_002=The soldiers were certainly baffled when not one of our group decided to place blame on another. With no evidence of disloyalty and impressed by our display of solidarity, we gained the approval of the conclave with a mutually beneficial arrangement.
BlameOut3_003=**Each player will gain 2 Resources** _(Knowledge or Ingredients)_ **of their choice at the start of the next Generation.**

# passages/00085-BlameResolve.mws.yaml
BlameResolve_001=Determined Resolution
BlameResolve_002=Weeks hence, we shared the disturbing occurrence of our military visitations with one another, unable to discern the significance. The ramifications of our decision would be made apparent soon enough, but we gave assurances to one another that if this gambit failed, we would discover another way to ensure that the fate of our estates would be secured.
BlameResolve_003=The player who chose to pay $2 to acquire a Flag token of the {warwinner} pays $2 and flips their token to the opposite side.
BlameResolve_004=Any player who chose to pay $2 to acquire a Flag token of the {warwinner} pays $2 and flips their token to the opposite side.

# passages/00086-RumorCreep.mws.yaml
RumorCreep_001=Curious Individual
RumorCreep_002=My intense curiosity was noted by the townspeople, and it appeared that my conversation with the vagrant had created a stir amongst the local gossips. I resolved to keep my meetings more clandestine in the future.
RumorCreep_003=**Gain 1VP** and **gain 1** {icon:creepy_icon}.

# passages/00087-RumorIngredient.mws.yaml
RumorIngredient_001=Procurement of Ingredients
RumorIngredient_002=A local farmer had observed my conversation, and after determining an agreeable moment to greet me, we engaged in a cordial chat about the local economy. The earthy individual even suggested a visit to his plantation, which turned out to be most advantageous.
RumorIngredient_003=**Gain 1 Ingredient of your choice.** _If it is a_ {icon:bodies_icon}_, gain 1_ {icon:creepy_icon}_._

# passages/00088-RumorKnowledge.mws.yaml
RumorKnowledge_001=Advancement of Knowledge
RumorKnowledge_002=While it seemed anomalous to me at the time, when my conversation ended I was immediately greeted by a fellow who introduced himself as one who shared an affinity for the scientific. I was intrigued and invited the young man in the brown sack suit to dine with me at a local cafe. Admittedly, my university knowledge was the main course, but I was still able to glean a few novel tidbits.
RumorKnowledge_003=**Gain 1 Knowledge of your choice.** _If it is "Occult", gain 1_ {icon:creepy_icon}_._

# passages/00089-RumorPitch.mws.yaml
RumorPitch_001=Dashing Conversationalist
RumorPitch_002=At university, I had always excelled at public speaking engagements. So when our conversation concluded, I spent the next few hours introducing myself to the less than charming group of locals that frequently attended political meetings. While they may not have fully comprehended the intelligence I exuded, there was certainly an air of cheerfulness when I exited the building.
RumorPitch_003=**Move the** {icon:angrymob_icon} **Marker one space to the right** and **gain 1VP**.

# passages/00090-CostStick.mws.yaml
CostStick_001=Good Fortune
CostStick_002=I could not determine why I had held onto such a grotesque, amateurish item. However, although I had no scientific basis for the assessment, it's presence appeared to provide an aura of good fortune. My endeavors were more easily bolstered and my resolution firmer upon viewing it.
CostStick_003=Any player with a {icon:s3_woodenfiguretoken} token returns it to the Scenario box and **gains 1 Resource** of their choice.

# passages/00091-ResistEnd2.mws.yaml
ResistEnd2_001=Financial Defenses
ResistEnd2_002=Advanced weaponry may turn the tide of a battle, but if the army has no monetary support to build and supply their troops with said defenses, the war will eventually be lost. It is this pledge of allegiance that inevitably determined the outcome of the war.
ResistEnd2_003=Count up how many {warwinner} Flag tokens total are face-up in all players' Estates. Then count up how many {warloser} Flag tokens total are face-up in all players' Estates. The army with the most Flag tokens wins the war. _(If there is a tie, the {warwinner} win the war.)_
ResistEnd2_004=Who won the war?
ResistEnd2_005=The {warwinner}
ResistEnd2_006=The {warloser}

# passages/00092-TTIntro3.mws.yaml
TTIntro3_001=To the Past
TTIntro3_002=As quickly as it had begun, the peculiar room fell silent. The door of the chamber fell from its hinges, flat to the earth, sparks and smoke billowing from the opening.
TTIntro3_003=We emerged from the mineshaft and made haste to the village. The changes were immediately obvious: The town had been returned to its former state, as it was in 1831. We knew that providence and some unseen benefactor had given us an opportunity to change the mistakes of the past and recreate a brighter future.
TTIntro3_004=I rushed to my Estate to be greeted by a familiar sight from my youth; the gothic iron and stone as formidable as I remembered. With a well-crafted farce, I introduced myself to my youthful parents as a relative on holiday. I quickly ingratiated myself into the fold and resolved to continue my experiments, searching for a way to return to my time, while also ensuring that history would not repeat itself.
TTIntro3_005=Time, it appeared, was not on my side.

# passages/00093-ParadoxFirst.mws.yaml
ParadoxFirst_001=New Science
ParadoxFirst_002=When I discovered the journal, the masterwork plans, and the clandestine fragments of experiments in the laboratory, I laughed. Surely, my great-grandfather had grandiose ambitions at the time, but modern advancements made many of the blueprints obsolete and frankly, a bit cute.
ParadoxFirst_003=I decided to improve upon them, and I knew just the thing that would dazzle them all!
ParadoxFirst_004=Retrieve the **Giant Masterwork** Experiments. Each player retrieves the matching Giant version of their Masterwork and returns their original Masterwork to the box. Any newly drawn Masterworks will now be chosen from their Giant versions.

# passages/00094-Weapons.mws.yaml
Weapons_001=Weapon Cache
Weapons_002=If you have any {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens remaining, **gain 1VP for each** {icon:s3_weapontoken} **token.**

# passages/00095-OUTDATEDFirstPara.mws.yaml
OUTDATEDFirstPara_001=Event introduced as HIGHER LEARNING originally...
OUTDATEDFirstPara_002=**University Dedication**
OUTDATEDFirstPara_003=**Experimental Bid**
OUTDATEDFirstPara_004=Bid with Highest VP on Experiment card.
OUTDATEDFirstPara_005=Dedicated in your Grandparent's name. Gain Upgrade of your choice from the line-up.

# passages/00096-TimeTokens.mws.yaml
TimeTokens_001=The Chance of Paradox
TimeTokens_002=Though they had been destroyed (or fully decayed) before I could witness their fabrication, I knew my presence could affect the natural order of things. I realized that, if the important experiments of the previous generation remained incomplete, the consequences were unknown and potentially catastrophic.
TimeTokens_003=Oh the chaotic potential this offered! I could not resist grinning.
TimeTokens_004=Retrieve the **Paradox** tokens {icon:s3_paradoxtoken}. Each player places 1 Paradox token {icon:s3_paradoxtoken} on each of their completed Experiments _(with the exception of their single stored Experiment)._
TimeTokens_005=Experiments with Paradox tokens {icon:s3_paradoxtoken} are considered **incomplete**. They can be completed with a Perform Experiment action as normal in order to return the token to the Scenario box.

# passages/00097-PeaceEventGas.mws.yaml
PeaceEventGas_001=Rule by Fear
PeaceEventGas_002=The ends justify the means. Through conquest of the world, we could finally enforce peace by removing the ills of humanity. The people would soon understand that without complete submission there would never be an end to conflict. With a few strategically placed charges, the gas filtered through the city. The massacre left thousands dead and countless citizens scarred permanently through the inhalation of the deadly chemical solution.
PeaceEventGas_003=In response to the clinical effectiveness of our actions, the government created a new department of **Public Relations** and asked for one of us to head the department.
PeaceEventGas_004=All players **gain 1** {icon:creepy_icon}, **1** {icon:insanity_icon}, and **an Ingredient of their choice.**

# passages/00098-PeaceEventNo.mws.yaml
PeaceEventNo_001=The Voice of the People
PeaceEventNo_002=While the confirmation of our own ethical standards both comforted and alarmed us, the military was forced to dispatch additional units to contain the uprising. This distraction was sufficient to significantly slow the advancement of troops across the continent as several minor uprisings were triggered and quashed in newly acquired territories.
PeaceEventNo_003=There is no bonus.

# passages/00099-OldManToken.mws.yaml
OldManToken_001=**A Fortuitous Letter?**
OldManToken_002=One morning under a swirling green sky, as I considered the viability of electrical conductivity for use as an incision tool in surgery, the caretaker discovered a small letter wrapped in twine upon my doorstep. As I hastily opened the note, it seemed to flicker wildly as if the time stream were resisting my actions.
OldManToken_003="Which flag do you fly?" _Which Flag token do you have?_

# passages/00100-OldManYes.mws.yaml
OldManYes_001=Underground Contacts
OldManYes_002=It seemed completely out of place to receive a letter detailing my grandparents significant impact within the resistance forces. The results spoke for themselves.
OldManYes_003=Upon unfolding the letter, I was surprised by its suddenly smooth surface and I dropped it onto the stone floor. While the words were still visible, they appeared to illuminate themselves from behind a clear pane of now fractured glass. When I lifted it again, the text scrolled with the motion of my thumb and a near endless supply of words were revealed to me. With this strange, future, electronic, mail in my laboratory I had no shortage of ideas!
OldManYes_004=Place the {figure} token near your Estate Affairs action. **When you take the Estate Affairs action to draw cards, do not discard.**

# passages/00101-OldManNo.mws.yaml
OldManNo_001=It was both a letter from the future written on bright, bleached stationary of an exceedingly fine consistency; and yet somehow also a ragged note scrawled in blood on a sheet of papyrus. I became fixated upon the deciphering the cryptic passages from two different times, spending countless hours attempting to stabilize it in some way.
OldManNo_002=But the task prove too daunting and too vexxing to complete! I threw it into the fires of my hearth in exasperation, only to watch it burn and cool itself in an endless loop. I lost much time and attention with my emotional reaction and I knew I should not have allowed the paradox to displace my emotions so boldly!
OldManNo_003=**Discard an Experiment card from your hand.**

# passages/00102-CostStick1.mws.yaml
CostStick1_001=Rediscovered Artist
CostStick1_002=An art critic arrived at my estate, and immediately took an enthusiastic interest in the misshapen wooden figure.
CostStick1_003=He explained his theory on the authenticity of the artistic piece: "His more well-known work in marble defined most of his career, however we believe that Ferenczy explored an abstract modernist period well before his contemporaries, with wooden figures." 
CostStick1_004=The collector offered me **$2** for the misshapen wooden figure, a sum that I gladly accepted in order to be rid of the hideous thing. 
CostStick1_005=Any player who has a {icon:s3_woodenfiguretoken} token returns it to the Scenario box and **gains $2**.

# passages/00104-CostStick2.mws.yaml
CostStick2_001=Ill Fortune
CostStick2_002=I could not determine why I had held onto such a grotesque, amateurish item. However, although I had no scientific basis for the assessment, it's presence appeared to provide an aura of ill fortune. My endeavours suffered and frustrations at my lack of productivity became a destructive force. I cast the figure into the fireplace in a fit, but the essence remained.
CostStick2_003=Any player with a **Wooden Figure** token returns it to the Scenario box and the **Storage Shed** has no effect for them at the start of this Generation.

# passages/00105-FutureStick.mws.yaml
FutureStick_001=The Key
FutureStick_002=I noticed that the misshapen wooden figure felt hollow inside. With a moment's hesitation, I cracked the object against the corner of the table. The contents spilled out upon the floor.
FutureStick_003=The object inside could not exist, and yet there it was. My mind was filled with questions that I knew might never be fully answered, but I was thankful for the assistance.
FutureStick_004=Any player who has a {icon:s3_woodenfiguretoken} token returns it to the Scenario box and takes an **Advanced Ingredient** of their choice.

# passages/00106-Paradoxical.mws.yaml
Paradoxical_001=Unexplainable Phenomenon
Paradoxical_002=There is no taming the wiles of time. History abhors a paradox. Though I did not fully understand the significance, fascinating oddities began to appear when loopholes were left untied.
Paradoxical_003=Retrieve the **Time Paradox** cards and shuffle them into a face-down deck. Each player draws a **Time Paradox** card for **each** {icon:s3_paradoxtoken} token in their possession.
Paradoxical_004=While most **Time Paradox** cards have a negative effect and are resolved immediately, some **Time Paradox** cards have special effects and must be kept face-up for the remainder of the Generation.

# passages/00107-Militarytoken.mws.yaml
Militarytoken_001=**Carefully give this Storybook device to the player with the {crest} token and do not allow any other players to see the screen.**
Militarytoken_002=**Duplicitous Duplicate**
Militarytoken_003=During a morning sojourn to the village, a confused man in military regalia hailed me from the across the street. While I assumed he must have mistaken me for someone else, he explained that he most definitely knew me and eagerly wanted to show me something. He insisted.
Militarytoken_004=I followed.
Militarytoken_005=I did Not follow.

# passages/00108-TownHallSpecial.mws.yaml
TownHallSpecial_001=Village Meeting
TownHallSpecial_002=While I attempted to divorce myself from trivial matters of politics, my spouse convinced me of the importance of understanding the mindset of the locals. So, one evening I accompanied my siblings to eschew our introspective tendencies and visit the Town Hall. The lively event intrigued us and we decided to investigate further.
TownHallSpecial_003=**Each player will now have an opportunity to talk to a person in the Town Hall.**

# passages/00109-TownHallS1.mws.yaml
TownHallS1_001=**Carefully hand this Storybook device to Player {_rnd_TownHallS1_0}**
TownHallS1_002=I decided to converse with:

# passages/00110-MilitaryYes.mws.yaml
MilitaryYes_001=Paradox Averted
MilitaryYes_002=Intrigued by his forwardness and familiarity, I followed him a few blocks to his home. Upon arrival, he opened the door and pointed to a {crest} figure. When I reached into my pocket, the same figure was there. 
MilitaryYes_003=Though my reflexes are exceedingly well-trained, I was caught unprepared when, spying the figure, the man's demeanor suddenly became fiery and with otherworldly speed he snatched it from my hands. As if compelled by an unseen force, he extended the {crest} towards the identical second figure. I witnessed his gloved hand, like a ghostly apparition, transition through it. Suddenly, the two identical pieces merged into one another seamlessly.
MilitaryYes_004=The man attempted to pull his fingers away, his entire frame beginning to shake and oscillate with a vicious intensity. I could sense a wave of heat radiating outward from the frightened indvidual, and scarcely shielded my eyes before the skin began to melt from his face like wax from a candle. Seconds later, his entire head exploded, the contents of which forcefully ejected themselves in a thick red ring across the walls of the room.
MilitaryYes_005=Certainly a great experiment on time paradoxes had been conducted today - though to what aim it served, I was not exactly certain.
MilitaryYes_006=**Discard an Experiment with a {icon:s3_paradoxtoken} token on it (also discard the token).** 
MilitaryYes_007=_If you have no {icon:s3_paradoxtoken} tokens, gain a {icon:s3_paradoxtoken} token and then discard it._

# passages/00111-MilitaryNo.mws.yaml
MilitaryNo_001=Compulsions
MilitaryNo_002=I calmly declined his invitation. Then, declined it again when he repeated his request. The man was enraged, his eyes transfixed seemingly on an object far away, though he stared in my direction.
MilitaryNo_003="I know who you are!" The animated man repeated as he was carried away by two police officers. His words were strained and disconcerting.
MilitaryNo_004=Later, I spoke to the officer at the sheriff's station in the Town Hall. With a few strategic white lies, I was able to negotiate the insane man's release and escorted him to my Estate discretely.
MilitaryNo_005=**Gain 1 {icon:bodies_icon}.** 
MilitaryNo_006=**Draw 2 Experiments** from the deck(s) of your choice.
MilitaryNo_007=Then, **gain a** {icon:s3_paradoxtoken} **token** and place it on one of your completed Experiments. _This Experiment counts as an incomplete Experiment and follows the_ {icon:s3_paradoxtoken} _token rules._

# passages/00112-Warwarn.mws.yaml
Warwarn_001=WARNING
Warwarn_002=Remove all player pieces from the board when performing the End of the Generation as normal, but do **NOT** discard your completed Experiments. You will still choose a completed Experiment to Store, but keep all your other completed Experiments nearby. 

# passages/00113-TimeWarp2.mws.yaml
TimeWarp2_001=Time Shifts Naturally
TimeWarp2_002=Whether my cousins and I dallied too long amongst the bounties of this alternate timeline or the universe required a reset, the mangled time-stream continued onward with or without my intervention.
TimeWarp2_004=**All players retrieve ALL their pieces from Lost** as their servants from the multiverses reappear to provide assistance.

# passages/00114-Stickfun.mws.yaml
Stickfun_001=**The Formation**
Stickfun_002=On a solitary afternoon in my study, I found my thoughts drifting to a curious object displayed on the mantle: the wooden figure whittled by a disturbed gentleman. However, as my gaze examined its surface, I noticed a curious indentation that appeared to be a frayed connection. I contacted my cousins to see if any others had acquired a similar object.
Stickfun_003=After consulting briefly with them, I realized that without another figure, I would never discover the secret. However, the figure did burn for an especially long time when I jettisoned it into the fireplace.
Stickfun_004=I used this time and warmth to reinvigorate my studies.
Stickfun_005=The player with the {icon:s3_woodenfiguretoken} returns it to the Scenario box and draws one Experiment card from the deck of their choice.
Stickfun_006=During a congenial supper visit, we discovered that the objects connected in a very specific pattern. With a metallic clicking sound, the pieces suddenly contorted into the broken form of a wooden man. The ligaments twisted wildly, and like a spider, the creature suddenly skittered up the walls, taking a defensive stance along the banister.
Stickfun_007=We were impressed, and with only one servant becoming horrible maimed in the process, we captured the beast and contributed it to the war effort.
Stickfun_008=Any player with a {icon:s3_woodenfiguretoken} token returns it to the Scenario box and gains 3 {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens.

# passages/00115-PlayerNameIntro.mws.yaml
PlayerNameIntro_005=As siblings of an influential family of Eastern European descent, the **{playtxt}** of us have received a not insignificant portion of our family's estate.
PlayerNameIntro_006=Before we begin, let us make this historical fiction more engaging by providing our names.

