# passages/00127-PackingHeat1.mws.yaml
PackingHeat1_001=Amassment of Weaponry
PackingHeat1_002=With the glorious schematics made into reality, I was able to test my weapons with great effect on the lands of my estate. However, with each crack of thunderous incendiaries, my bold new vision for modern arms attracted further attention, for better or worse.
PackingHeat1_003=Choose the name of the player who completed **2 Advanced Weaponry** Experiments:

# passages/00128-PackingHeat1a.mws.yaml
PackingHeat1a_001=Attracting Attentions
PackingHeat1a_002=While the {warwinner} were critical of my efforts (or jealous), the {warloser} were keen to curry my favor. Of course, I was not surprised. If I were in their shoes - quivering deprostrate in the presence of genius - I would surely hope to gain my notice as well.
PackingHeat1a_003=1 {icon:creepy_icon} and 1 Resource of their choice.
PackingHeat1a_004=1 Resource of their choice and moves the {icon:angrymob_icon} Marker 1 space to the left.
PackingHeat1a_005={heat} gains {_rnd_PackingHeat1a_0}
PackingHeat1a_006=If they have not already done so, {heat} may flip their Flag token to the {warloser} side if they wish.

# passages/00131-TownHallOpposite.mws.yaml
TownHallOpposite_001=On a brisk April morning, our parents were called upon to attend another Town Hall meeting. Knowing full well the outcome, I summoned my cousins and concocted a simple plan to avoid the same mistake as the past. Using a mercurial and chloroform solution, our families were sufficiently lethargic upon the day in question and could not attend.
TownHallOpposite_002=We arrived in their place as surrogates and proceeded to vote counter to what we had before.
TownHallOpposite_003=Because of our decision, the **Barracks are built in town**. Whatever escalating tension had occurred in the original timeline was mended, or at least it was dulled.
TownHallOpposite_004=Because of our decision, the **Barracks are not built in town**. Whatever escalating tension had occurred in the original timeline was mended, or at least it was dulled.

# passages/00132-TownNameEntry.mws.yaml
TownNameEntry_001=Welcome to the village of
TownNameEntry_002={townname}.
TownNameEntry_003=We hope you enjoy your stay.

# passages/00134-AfternoonTea.mws.yaml
AfternoonTea_001=Afternoon Tea
AfternoonTea_004=It was absolutely dreadful. Astringent tea from an obscure area of the orient - bitter, stale cranberry scones, wildflower honey, and store-bought cream - this was without question the worst tea party to which I had ever had the displeasure of an invitation. And to think, the Monarchy was responsible for such a wasted afternoon.
AfternoonTea_005=What kind of aristocracy was this? It made me re-evaluate my position entirely. If I could be served indigestible digestives then perhaps I should cause the nobility a little indigestion in response by burning down the {teaopt}! It would certainly remove the requirement to visit.
AfternoonTea_006=However, a plan as critical as this one required a conspiracy to execute. Therefore, regretably, the fate of the operation was left to the whims of my family, whom I loved dearly.

# passages/00135-ReignIntro.mws.yaml
ReignIntro_001=Visit with the Royal Advisor
ReignIntro_002=The royal advisor had anticipated my visit and breathed a sigh of relief when I entered. Clearly the responsibility did not suit him. I was all too happy to encourage that attitude.
ReignIntro_003=The new Unified Monarchist building felt distinctly out of place in the town center - as distant in tone and architecture as the royal capitol from the countryside. The royal advisor himself was similarly off kilter. He was a portly man of considerable age with a gray moustache, stiff and twirled. His bright clothes ballooned in all directions.
ReignIntro_004=I had sent a brief correspondence in advance, so I signed the guest book and entered quickly with practiced etiquette.

