# passages/00149-IntroConflict.mws.yaml
IntroConflict_001=War on the Horizon
IntroConflict_002=The spectre of war haunted the small village. This ideological tension would erupt in loud displays and gatherings of the peasantry near the Town Hall. For all the folderol, I began to cherish the moments when the eerie stillness of the evening was broken by anguished yells.
IntroConflict_003=The Separatists felt alienated by the aristocratic government and wished to secede. Their brash tactics aimed to incite a democratic revolt among the proletariat. The Unified Monarchists feared the anarchic destabilization of the economy at such a key moment during industrialization. I was quickly able to determine that **the town supported the {warwinner}**.
IntroConflict_004=Place the {warwinner} Flag card face-up near the Village Chronicle.

# passages/00150-ParadoxTimeRandom.mws.yaml
ParadoxTimeRandom_001=**A Surge of Productivity**
ParadoxTimeRandom_002=The time device proved to be invaluable for productivity. While the general populace squabbled over self-interests, creating and destroying the countryside in equal measure with varying degrees of incalculable existential horror, I was generally left to my leisure in solitude with my spouse and servants.
ParadoxTimeRandom_003=One flick of an electrical switch and the copper fixtures of the device sent me back to the moments before a failed experiment. I soon became acquainted with visitations from myself, even sharing tea with several versions of my person to talk over and revise a particularly difficult thesis. While the process aged me quicker than desired, the ingredients it saved and the excellent conversation proved well worth it.
ParadoxTimeRandom_004=**A Clarity of Purpose**
ParadoxTimeRandom_005=Technological advancement retrieved from the future, the stability offered by knowing you can change your past, the ability to travel backwards in time to guide one's self away from a rough day ahead; general access to a time machine could lift a near Utopia right to the edge of perfection!
ParadoxTimeRandom_006=While I was somewhat disappointed in the lack of chaos, I was ecstatic at the reaction of the university elite. Our decision had such a positive effect on the world, it made the academics positively seethe! Those furrowed brows and anxious worry lines grafted onto their imbecilic faces made the outcome of this rash decision a joy to behold. It wasn't long before this joy gave way to clarity of purpose. I felt reinvigorated, hoping each day that my next experiment would evoke the same horrific response.
ParadoxTimeRandom_007=**None Left Behind**
ParadoxTimeRandom_008=If I were to forgo humility for a moment and describe one of my most favorable traits, I am a creature of infinite patience. So, I watched as the first experiments in time alteration bore miniscule results and continued in my tasks without paying them much heed. Like all initial fascinations, the wave of interest in manipulating fate slowly gave way to other technological distractions and time machines became popular children's toys around the holidays.
ParadoxTimeRandom_009=I cannot recollect the moment when I noticed it, perhaps it happened naturally, but as the timeline shifted ever so slowly, it appeared that the forces aligning the cosmos preferred stasis over the whims of chaos. With each passing season, the studious gap between myself and my cousins seemed to edge ever closer.
ParadoxTimeRandom_010=And though I abhorred the thought of intervention from forces outside of my understanding, I cannot say that I did not relish my stoicism being rewarded.
ParadoxTimeRandom_011=**Future Notes**
ParadoxTimeRandom_012=There are narrative consequences for unleashing a Time Machine into the wild, and the devastation is too far-reaching for one single paragraph in a mad scientist's memoir to detail. However, it has **no effect on gameplay** and therefore will be omitted. 
ParadoxTimeRandom_013=It is better to write these words now in anticipation of the game, My Father's Work, which will see release in 2022 and detail the historical events of my family. I've played it a few times during my travels and while I wish it had a solo version, it's still very good. 
ParadoxTimeRandom_014=Perhaps history will no longer align with the narrative presented in the game and this paragraph will seem oddly out of place. Ah, such is the confounding nature of time travel.
ParadoxTimeRandom_015=**Trust and Benevolence**
ParadoxTimeRandom_016=The people have developed a sense of trust and acceptance for my work after the unmitigated success of the time altering apparatus. Trust and acceptance? I grapple with this concept with many of my waking hours. Even on the days where I feel emboldened to venture backwards into the timestream to undo this stomach-turning adoration, some peon in the village simply undoes my work.
ParadoxTimeRandom_017=My beautifully macabre estate is now looked upon with exuberance by tourists to the region. Tourists! By god, this will make pushing the boundaries of ethical imagination nearly impossible! I must break through this irrational barrier of love and generosity before it stifles my work!
ParadoxTimeRandom_018=**A Return to Suspicion**
ParadoxTimeRandom_019=How could they accuse us of sedition? The Time Machine was my family's gift to all of humanity and yet they call it willfully negligent and unethical!
ParadoxTimeRandom_020=Do we blame Prometheus for every home burnt to the ground because of the invention of fire? Is the zoetrope responsible for every detestable piece of film created after it? Should we ban perfumes and colognes for their ability to more fervently entice couples into intimacy? It is only natural that the most important discoveries carry with them a modicum of insidious potential.
ParadoxTimeRandom_021=It is absurd that a correlative effect is so readily pinned upon me. Yet, their superstitions have once again returned! 
ParadoxTimeRandom_022=**Targeted**
ParadoxTimeRandom_023=They discovered who did it. Hungarian government tracked it. 
ParadoxTimeRandom_024=Perhaps it was easy to discern this information as every pamphlet, editorial, journal, and detailed blueprint was signed in bold ink. It was all for naught as well. The Hungarian government quietly tracked each copy down with the assistance of the scientific community, and secured this knowledge for themselves alone.
ParadoxTimeRandom_025=My family's decision to disseminate this information had dire consequences for those that chose this path. Their Masterwork was rendered pointless to complete as it would be confiscated immediately by police force emboldened by access to the time stream. Fortunately, those that decided to remain silent could not be implicated merely by association and remained free to continue their work.
ParadoxTimeRandom_026=**Utter Catastrophe**
ParadoxTimeRandom_027=There is always a cycle of destruction and renewal with every major epoch in the world's history, and this would probably be seen as a minor stumbling block in the overall chronology of events. With the ease of general access to a device that had the power to bend time and space around it, it was soon discovered that the average individual may have lacked the self-control and intelligence required to prevent the catastrophic destruction of nearly every living thing in Eastern Europe. 
ParadoxTimeRandom_028=Owning an Estate made of stone, looming high above the valley, I was able to retain most of my possessions. Although the air was now tinged with a hint of sulfur and resources were a touch harder to procure.
ParadoxTimeRandom_029=This was a minor setback.
ParadoxTimeRandom_030=All players **draw a C-level Experiment** and immediately place it into their **Stored Experiments**. Do not gain any VP, penalties, or rewards for this experiment. It counts as a Completed C-level Experiment.
ParadoxTimeRandom_031=All players immediately move their {icon:insanity_icon} marker to the starting space. Then, all players gain 1 Compulsion.
ParadoxTimeRandom_032=Each player immediately **gains 2VP for each other player token** ahead of them on the VP track.
ParadoxTimeRandom_033=Nothing happens. However, the emotions the players feel at this lack of chaos affecting the game is very real, I'm sure.
ParadoxTimeRandom_034=All players **lose** 1 {icon:creepy_icon} for each Estate upgrade with a {icon:creepy_icon} on it. _If this would cause a player to retreat to the left past the {figure} token, they must return a Vanity Estate Upgrade to the supply._
ParadoxTimeRandom_035=Retrieve the Angry Mob marker and place it on the space on the Creepy Track with the {figure} token. Then return the {figure} token to the scenario box. The original Angry Mob rules are in effect again. 
ParadoxTimeRandom_036=_If any player has already reached or exceeded this space on the Angry Mob track, they must return a Vanity Estate Upgrade to the supply._
ParadoxTimeRandom_037={nameA} must flip their Giant Masterwork face-down.
ParadoxTimeRandom_038={nameB} must flip their Giant Masterwork face-down.
ParadoxTimeRandom_039={nameC} must flip their Giant Masterwork face-down.
ParadoxTimeRandom_040={nameD} must flip their Giant Masterwork face-down.
ParadoxTimeRandom_041={nameE} must flip their Giant Masterwork face-down.
ParadoxTimeRandom_042=Any player with a face-down Masterwork can no longer complete it this Generation. _If you have already completed it, immediately lose an amount of VP equal to the completion value on the front side and gain 3 Resources (ingredient, knowledge, or money) from the supply._
ParadoxTimeRandom_043=Turn to page **22** of the Village Chronicle.
ParadoxTimeRandom_044=Return the **In Memoriam** upgrade tile to the scenario box. Return the **{figure} token** to the scenario box.

# passages/00151-IntroMartial-Monarchists.mws.yaml
IntroMartial_Monarchists_001=Plagued by Conflict
IntroMartial_Monarchists_002=If one can call the prospect of perpetual conflict stabilizing, my life settled into a somewhat steady routine. During the day, the sound of distant gunfire rumbled through the halls of my estate as silver plumes of smoke billowed beyond the mountainous horizon, casting tendril-like shadows across the land — a constant reminder of civil war. At night, the rare spectacle of an explosion brightening the sky surprised me with how viscerally I reacted.
IntroMartial_Monarchists_003=Soldiers in their bright regalia keep watch over the town from a newly erected outpost, waving the brilliant orange flag of royalty. The Monarchy had claimed victory from afar after stationing their ranks across the region, but as scuffles remained constant, this declaration was all pomp without substance. The Monarchy drafted citizens into their ranks and levied penalties against those who showed disloyalty.
IntroMartial_Monarchists_004=The inference that one of my standing should owe a debt of servitude to those who already tax my earnings into oblivion was enough to make me spill my tea. And to what end, I wondered? Could peace be mustered in a populace kept so distant from the individuals who ruled it? It was called the industrial revolution for a reason, was it not?
IntroMartial_Monarchists_005=But, I must admit, the safety that the Monarchy afforded appealed to my pocketbook. Appeasing the Monarchy would ensure money and influence, but it also appeared — for better or ill — that royalty was distant enough to take little interest in our experimentations unless they provided direct benefit to themselves, whereas the Separatists were interested in knowledge and were desperate to explore all scientific options available to them to turn the tide. However, their frail sensibilities would not so easily accept my experimentations. 
IntroMartial_Monarchists_006=Ah, to be left to one's own devices or to be famously scrutinized, reviled, and revered in equal measure! The decision weighed upon me so heavily it gave me mild indigestion during my evening banquets. What direction should I choose to advance my most important scientific work? 

# passages/00152-IntroMartial-Separatists.mws.yaml
IntroMartial_Separatists_001=Down with the Monarchy
IntroMartial_Separatists_002=The length and difficulty of my journey was exacerbated by the ongoing conflict. Compounding this harried inconvenience, my spouse and I suffered the indignity of a lengthy interrogation by soldiers of the Separatist forces, who had imposed an unofficial martial government. 
IntroMartial_Separatists_003=Peasants-turned-soldiers in their motley uniforms keep watch over the town from a newly erected outpost waving a sanguine flag. They spoke of freedom as they dug fresh graves in the cemetery; the wrought iron gates perpetually wreathed in lilies. I observed the daily horse-drawn carts, dragging the wounded towards ill-equipped infirmaries; my crimson reflection in the muddy ruts of unpaved highways.
IntroMartial_Separatists_004=It was both in spite of and because of this brashness that I found myself drawn to the scrappy Separatist upstarts and their eagerness to fight for the capricious whims of the great unwashed. The Separatists were desperate for the advantages that my family's experimentations provided, and while hesitant over our methods, were willing to further our knowledge in return. Unfortunately, this relationship made them more entitled to levy accusations towards us.
IntroMartial_Separatists_005=However, the influence of the throne was still absolute. If one could ingratiate themselves with the distracted Monarchy, their influence and money was on offer. The peasantry would be too discontent to focus on our more "ambitious" works. Unfortunately, unless experimentation directly benefited them, the Monarchy had no use for it.
IntroMartial_Separatists_006=Ah, to be left to one's own devices or to be famously scrutinized, reviled, and revered in equal measure! The decision weighed upon me so heavily that I could scarcely enjoy my afternoon pastries. Neither could the muffled wailing coming from the cellar laboratory nor the distant clattering of gunfire at night calm my weary mind. What direction should I choose to advance my most important scientific work? 

# passages/00153-RoyalBarnCheck.mws.yaml
RoyalBarnCheck_002=The Unified Monarchists are furious to discover that one of our family has been consorting with the enemy for over a decade. I am adamant in my disapproval of my father's hidden grudge against the current government and I offer them access to all goods within, free of charge. I am forever a proud citizen of this nation and harbor absolutely no ill-feelings, nor grudges which will spitefully fester in my psyche for the remainder of my years.
RoyalBarnCheck_003=**The player with the "Suspicious Barn" must flip it face-down until Game End Scoring. It will be scored as an Estate Upgrade, but it's ability can no longer be used.**

# passages/00154-SeparatistBarnCheck.mws.yaml
SeparatistBarnCheck_001=The Separatists were furious to discover that one of our family had been consorting with the enemy for over a decade. I was adamant in my disapproval of my father's hidden grudge against the current government and I offered them access to all goods within, free of charge. I am forever a proud citizen of this nation and harbor absolutely no ill-feelings nor grudges which could spitefully fester in my psyche for the remainder of my years.
SeparatistBarnCheck_002=**The player with the "Suspicious Barn" must flip it face-down until Game End Scoring. It will be scored as an Estate Upgrade, but its ability can no longer be used.**

# passages/00155-1stCrownCons.mws.yaml
_1stCrownCons_001=The Queen's Ire
_1stCrownCons_002=To be the **first** to invoke the ire of the crown by becoming too close was a mistake I had never intended to make. The Queen had taken notice of my ambitions, a fact that I could surmise from the increased frequency of visits from the local guard. Each day, I spied the flash of an orange military uniform as they kept watch over my hillside abode.
_1stCrownCons_003=How could I have been so bold? Why did they hound me so? It was enough to rattle the nerves to the point that I even found myself destroying the evidence of my work in a bout of mania. But I continued onward, knowing that my intellect was too fierce to be contained! Look upon me if you wish, I will rise to fight again!
_1stCrownCons_004=**Lose 3VP** and **discard an Experiment card** from your hand back to the supply.
_1stCrownCons_005=Remove your {icon:creepy_icon} Marker from the {icon:creepy_icon} Track and place it on top of your Score Track Marker.

# passages/00156-RoyalDecreeExplain.mws.yaml
RoyalDecreeExplain_001=Royal Power
RoyalDecreeExplain_011=While my influence was no longer as direct as a {_rnd_RoyalDecreeExplain_0} or a {_rnd_RoyalDecreeExplain_1} appearing on the battlefield in all their glory, a pocket full of coin and a persuasive meal could also perform similarly with the right individual. That individual just so happened to be stationed in the newly built Unified Monarchist property in town. I would find myself frequenting this office when I wanted to redirect the oppression of local policies from the crown.
RoyalDecreeExplain_012=**Exercising Royal Decrees**
RoyalDecreeExplain_013=Anytime you visit the **Royal Advisor** and pay $1, you will be given the opportunity to make a Royal Decree that will affect the region.
RoyalDecreeExplain_014=The player who performs the **most Decrees** will receive a bonus at the End of the Generation.

