# passages/00160-ATOWSabotage1.mws.yaml
ATOWSabotage1_001=The Choice for Resistance
ATOWSabotage1_002=I could not be swayed. It was clear that my most moral and proper duty was to oppose tyranny in all forms. Though I shuddered at the means by which this task would be accomplished, I knew first-hand how motivational a force fear could be.
ATOWSabotage1_003=**The choice was clear:**
ATOWSabotage1_004=The Barracks was a worthy target for my most righteous sabotage.
ATOWSabotage1_005=The Laborer's Union was a worthy target for my most righteous sabotage.
ATOWSabotage1_006=Laborer's Union

# passages/00161-ATOWSabotageConfirm.mws.yaml
ATOWSabotageConfirm_002=I penned a letter to my contact within the {warloser}. The site had been chosen and the {bldg1} would fall, weakening the {warwinner}' position in the village.

# passages/00162-ATOWSabotageIntro1.mws.yaml
ATOWSabotageIntro1_001=**Carefully hand this Storybook device to the player with the fewest VP.** _(If tied, the one latest in turn order in the previous round.)_ **Do not allow any other players to see the screen.**
ATOWSabotageIntro1_004=It was time to strike while my passions were still agitated! But, was it in my best interest to turn my destructive gaze towards the {warloser}' noble cause? Or perhaps one of my kin could stand to be targeted by my ire?
ATOWSabotageIntro1_007=I chose to sabotage one of my cousins.

# passages/00163-ATOWSabotageMonConfirm.mws.yaml
ATOWSabotageMonConfirm_001=I penned a letter to my contact within the {warloser}. The site had been chosen and the {bldg2} would fall, weakening the {warwinner} position in the village.

# passages/00165-CommemorativeStatueEvent.mws.yaml
CommemorativeStatueEvent_001=Royal Eyes Upon Us
CommemorativeStatueEvent_002=While I shuddered at the thought of attracting too much attention to my activities in case they would be mistaken for deviance, I was unable to resist the gaze of noble adoration. With my frequent **visits to the Royal Advisor**, a rare - I struggle to say it - 'friendship' blossomed. With the regional influence wielded by the gentleman, he proposed a substantial gift in my honor - a statue at the center of a newly fashioned park within the city limits.
CommemorativeStatueEvent_003=Of course, this "gift" was not free. And with my cousins vying for similar attentions, it would require a bit of persuasion to receive this monument in my honor. The landmark meant little to me, of course, but to leave an indelible reminder of my family's bounteous contributions for all to see, that alone would provide me solace.

# passages/00166-CommemorativeSignIn.mws.yaml
CommemorativeSignIn_001=Memorial Observance
CommemorativeSignIn_002=It was both a marvelous testament to the scientific spirit and a bitter eyesore sculpted from marred stone by amateur architects. My humility would not allow me to view it in a truly positive light. Yet, as frivolous as it was, it was vital in imprinting the legacy of my most revered family upon the region. 
CommemorativeSignIn_003=**Which player visited the Commemorative Statue today?**

# passages/00167-CommemorativeMAIN.mws.yaml
CommemorativeMAIN_001=Unyielding Inspiration
CommemorativeMAIN_002=Although the craftmanship was amateurish and the marble of lower grade than expected, I was once again stunned into silence as I arrived to marvel at the statue. What it lacked in polish, it excelled in artistic passion!
CommemorativeMAIN_003=The picturesque monument always set my heart beating and drove me to tears. Sobbing into my handkerchief, I could feel the doubts melt away.
CommemorativeMAIN_004=What an inspiration! 
CommemorativeMAIN_005={signincomm} may perform **one** of two available actions:
CommemorativeMAIN_006=Lose 2 {icon:insanity_icon}.
CommemorativeMAIN_007=Lose 2 {icon:creepy_icon} and move the {icon:s3_crowntoken} token 1 space in the direction of your choice.

# passages/00168-CommemorativeOTHER.mws.yaml
CommemorativeOTHER_001=Bitter Eyesore
CommemorativeOTHER_002=as I ventured nearer the dismal, gray statue.
CommemorativeOTHER_003=as a chill wind swept debris about the cracked foundation.
CommemorativeOTHER_004=How could they construct such a ghastly structure in the vague form of an unworthy clod? The thought set my features to crease into an ugly snear{_rnd_CommemorativeOTHER_0}
CommemorativeOTHER_005=And yet, set upon by the emotional heft of this abomination, I felt at once reinvigorated. For while love in its most passionate form was known to revive the soul, it is hate which raises the blood to the cheeks and sets the mind to precise action. I spoke a curse so vile I felt the lilacs wilt at the base of the wretched monument and spat upon the ground thrice.
CommemorativeOTHER_006=My cousin may have enjoyed their victory in that moment, but soon I would be the one standing upon the pedestal... the pedestal of science!
CommemorativeOTHER_007={signincomm} may search an Experiment deck and draw the card of their choice. _Reshuffle the deck afterwards._

