# passages/00172-ATOW-FamineEvent.mws.yaml
ATOW_FamineEvent_001=Famine
ATOW_FamineEvent_002=Because of the rapid expansion of war efforts, stocks of goods were increasingly hard to come by. When a famine struck in 1901, the food shortages caused mass riots. Ideas were thrown about for potential solutions - labor camps for dissidents, re-education facilities, pills that slow the metabolism - but all of these were bandages that did not address the root of the issue.
ATOW_FamineEvent_003=While I offered it in jest at first, the most clean, efficient, and logical course was to utilize what we now had in droves to offset what we lacked. Were we to simply riddle our enemy's bodies with bullets and let them spoil the soil? Why should we allow perfectly good protein to waste away in the elements?
ATOW_FamineEvent_004=I decided to convene with my cousins and put the matter to a vote.
ATOW_FamineEvent_005=We could continue to provide empty promises of more food in the future and preach hardiness and austerity. Or we could provide a **real**, sustainable solution that would guarantee success on the battlefield.

# passages/00173-RoyalPriceisRight.mws.yaml
RoyalPriceisRight_001=Royally Adjacent
RoyalPriceisRight_002=With such direct access to royalty, it was mere weeks before I garnered a curious intrigue for my work. I knew this notoriety would serve my purposes well and shield me from scrutiny of my more unscrupulous designs. 
RoyalPriceisRight_003=However, intrigue is what I desired. Suspicions, I did not. I aimed to remain like a whispering shadow, a ghostly hand so close as to curry favor and power, yet far enough removed to not arouse undesired attention. With such dark work to be done, it would require a deft and meticulous hand. And as luck would have it, this was precisely what I was born to do.
RoyalPriceisRight_004=Return the **Suspicion** and {icon:angrymob_icon} Markers to the game box. Retrieve the {icon:s3_crowntoken} token and place it on space **{tracker}** of the {icon:creepy_icon} Track.
RoyalPriceisRight_005=At the End of this Generation, the player(s) closest to the {icon:s3_crowntoken} token on the {icon:creepy_icon} Track without overlapping or exceeding it will **gain 6VP**.
RoyalPriceisRight_006=However, if a player's token ever overlaps or exceeds the {icon:s3_crowntoken} token, there will be permanent negative consequences for them.

# passages/00174-AfternoonTeaResolutionYAY.mws.yaml
AfternoonTeaResolutionYAY_001=A Destructive Success
AfternoonTeaResolutionYAY_002=The {teaopt} was no match for the power of our well-orchestrated combined experimental talents. Did the series of clamorous explosions arouse suspicions? Perhaps. But the fanfare certainly offered the townsfolk new inspiration to rally towards the cause.
AfternoonTeaResolutionYAY_003=With minimal casualties, the Barracks had been turned to rubble. No longer would we be beholden to the tyrannous edict of forced conscription.
AfternoonTeaResolutionYAY_004=Move the {icon:angrymob_icon} Marker **1 space** to the left.
AfternoonTeaResolutionYAY_005=Move the {icon:angrymob_icon} Marker **2 spaces** to the left.
AfternoonTeaResolutionYAY_006=All players must discard a completed Experiment card back to the supply.
AfternoonTeaResolutionYAY_007=All players who voted **NAY lose 2** {icon:creepy_icon} and may draw an **Advanced Weaponry** card.

# passages/00175-AfternoonTeaResolutionNAY.mws.yaml
AfternoonTeaResolutionNAY_001=Conspiracy Failed
AfternoonTeaResolutionNAY_002=My altruistic nature would not allow me to seek revenge on such trivial matters when my great work was primed to change the world. Of course, I attempted to dissuade my dear cousin from this rash course of action, but I was unsuccessful. Expectedly, their dubious manners and overt schemes were not well-received by the local officials. It was fortunate that our illustrious grandfather were not here to see this pathetic display. I am sure he is seething in his coffin over it even now!
AfternoonTeaResolutionNAY_003=I could not fault my cousins for their decision. It is sometimes a struggle for those with unfortunately low intellect to execute on a scheme. The afternoon tea incident would forever remain unavenged.
AfternoonTeaResolutionNAY_004=The player who did not win the bid **gains 2** {icon:creepy_icon} and may draw an **Advanced Weaponry** card.
AfternoonTeaResolutionNAY_005=All players who voted **YAY** **gain 1** {icon:creepy_icon} and may draw an **Advanced Weaponry** card.

# passages/00176-VariableList-ATOW.mws.yaml
VariableList_ATOW_001=General
VariableList_ATOW_002={players} Player count
