# passages/00177-Player1BeenSabotaged.mws.yaml
Player1BeenSabotaged_001=**Carefully hand this Storybook device to {sabotagee1}. Do not allow any other players to see the screen.**
Player1BeenSabotaged_002=**A Noble Retort**
Player1BeenSabotaged_003=Being a learned individual of noble birth, I am not one easily moved towards aggression. My passions are passions of scholarly determination and intellectual exploration. But when it was made known to me that {playersabotage1} was behind the deplorable physical attack upon my estate, I knew it was my firm duty to respond directly.
Player1BeenSabotaged_004=As a stabled horse would swat away a fly with its tail, my cousin's woeful and inadequate betrayal barely registered upon my thoughts. Yet when I consulted with my barrister, they deemed it necessary that I should issue a sternly worded statement of purpose. Otherwise, I would not be properly protecting my own interests, of course.
Player1BeenSabotaged_005=**I decided that in response to their treachery:**
Player1BeenSabotaged_006=I would seek satisfaction 
Player1BeenSabotaged_007=through a duel.
Player1BeenSabotaged_008= _(This could result in death or loss of VP.)_
Player1BeenSabotaged_010=formally denounce these juvenile antics.
Player1BeenSabotaged_011= _(Through a strongly-worded letter.)_

# passages/00178-DuelRules1.mws.yaml
DuelRules1_001=Rules of the Duel
DuelRules1_002=Over the next few days, I formalized the rules of engagement for a duel that would take place as soon as all parties were able. I knew that I could choose a duel of **scientific prowess** or **pistols** at twenty paces.
DuelRules1_003=A scientific duel would be a duel where we would compare our research and skill levels in one of four scientific fields to be determined randomly. By adding our total Journal Track levels to our completed Experiments of that type, we would determine the victor! 
DuelRules1_004=A duel with pistols would be a duel where the victor was determined through sheer chance.
DuelRules1_005=I chose a battle of wits.
DuelRules1_007=I chose pistols at dawn.
DuelRules1_008=pistols
DuelRules1_009=Or perhaps, I chose to retract and 
DuelRules1_010=send them a strongly-worded letter.

# passages/00179-DuelDenounce1.mws.yaml
DuelDenounce1_001=**Carefully hand the Storybook to {playersabotage1}. This passage is then read aloud to all players.**
DuelDenounce1_002=**Firm Rebuke**
DuelDenounce1_003=I remember the morning upon which the letter arrived with the stand-up wash. With the scent of rosemary in my freshly sponged hair, a sordid disappointment came upon me. The stern words of my kin were filled with all the pomposity of a marching band and yet issued no official challenge or retort whatsoever. The matter had been settled through alternative means, and my virtuous name amongst the scientific establishment, though stained by my provocative actions, only saw the smallest of setbacks.
DuelDenounce1_004=Perhaps I had craved the excitement of an escalation between myself and my cousin. Or maybe it was the competitive nature of true science and discovery that stirred my lust for familial discontent. It served no purpose to dwell on it further however. The matter was settled and I soon found myself absorbed in my work once again.
DuelDenounce1_005={playersabotage1} gains **1** {icon:creepy_icon} and loses **1VP**.

# passages/00180-AcceptDuel1.mws.yaml
AcceptDuel1_001=**Carefully hand this Storybook device to {playersabotage1}. Do not allow any other players to see the screen.**
AcceptDuel1_002=**Code Duello**
AcceptDuel1_003=I remember the morning upon which the letter arrived with the stand-up wash. With the scent of rosemary in my freshly sponged hair, my hackles raised and I toppled the warm basin to the floor in my rage! My own cousin, inviting me to a **duel**!
AcceptDuel1_004=This duel of **{dueltype}** would 
AcceptDuel1_005=randomly determine a victor through sheer chance.
AcceptDuel1_006=compare our Journal Track and Experiments in one of four scientific fields. This field would be determined randomly on the day of the duel.
AcceptDuel1_007=**With little deliberation, I put my quill to the page and responded:**
AcceptDuel1_008=accept this duel.
AcceptDuel1_009=decline this duel.

# passages/00181-DuelDecline1.mws.yaml
DuelDecline1_001=Letter of Apology
DuelDecline1_002=While my dear cousin was clearly the guilty party in this arrangement, I had more profitable matters with which to attend. The magnitude and scope were far greater than a simple matter of he-said, she-said.
DuelDecline1_003=I chose to be the greater individual and issued a formal apology for whatever offenses I had hitherto caused - without legal admittance of guilt - absolving myself of the duty to duel entirely. I hoped that this would spare any needless grudges or hard feelings in the future.
DuelDecline1_004={playersabotage1} gains **1** {icon:creepy_icon}.

# passages/00182-DuelResolution1.mws.yaml
DuelResolution1_001=**This and the subsequent passages are revealed and read aloud to all players.**
DuelResolution1_002=**The Bloody Business**
DuelResolution1_003=As quick as the sun rose above the Carpathian Mountains, the morning of the dreaded duel had arrived. I was eager to settle this business and return home to my laboratory, but not so eager as to miss removing the arrogant smirk from my cousin's lips.
DuelResolution1_004=I once again checked the chamber of my pistol, seeing a single polished bullet stationed inside. With a deep breath, I engaged the firing pin with my thumb and holstered the weapon at my side. It was then that I felt the beating of my heart as a chill ran down my spine. I was ready to end this bloody business.
DuelResolution1_005=I opened the hatch on my carriage, allowing a fresh plume of acrid smoke to billow into the open, revealing my managerie of scientific equipment. I was ready to conduct some true science!
DuelResolution1_006=Click to begin the duel...
DuelResolution1_010=Occult

# passages/00183-DuelResolution1a.mws.yaml
DuelResolution1a_001=The Moment of Truth
DuelResolution1a_002=At a distance of twenty paces, I turned and fired. I heard the report of two shots before a cloud of smoke blurred my vision. In my shocked state, I could not determine if this was two clear shots or the single bullet from my own chamber and the echo of its blast shattering the stillness of the morning.
DuelResolution1a_003=The scientific duel will be **{duelsci}**.
DuelResolution1a_004={sabotagee1} and {playersabotage1} now count how many Levels they have moved their Journal Track forward in {duelsci}.
DuelResolution1a_005=They then count how many of their completed Experiments (including stored) are of the type {duelsci}.
DuelResolution1a_006=Each player adds these two numbers together to determine their total individual scientific prowess. _(For example, Level 1 in {duelsci} plus 2 completed {duelsci} Experiments would equal a total of 3.)_

# passages/00184-DuelResolution1b.mws.yaml
DuelResolution1b_001=An Unfortunate Death
DuelResolution1b_002=Wounded Pride
DuelResolution1b_003=I watched as my opponent, {duelloser}
DuelResolution1b_004= burst into tears. Apparently my bullet had struck their shoulder, causing a rip in the fabric and minor cut. Unable to stomach the pain, they
DuelResolution1b_005= red-faced, turned to a new page in their occult tome and feigned a paper-cut so egregious that they
DuelResolution1b_006= suddenly complained of a strained wrist as their pitiful, makeshift contraption grinded to a halt. They
DuelResolution1b_007= held the side of their arm where a chemical burn had reddened the skin and
DuelResolution1b_008= grimaced, exposing a deep wound in their forearm as the modified falcon under their care flew far into the distance. They
DuelResolution1b_009= stumbled to their doctor. While their injuries from the duel were minor, I felt a deep fulfillment in knowing that their insufferable pride had been dealt a cruel blow that morning.
DuelResolution1b_011={duelloser} loses **3VP**.
DuelResolution1b_012=Though I felt a tinge of remorse at the sight, my cousin and I were both aware of the fatal risks this bloody confrontation carried with it. I watched spellbound as {duelloser} 
DuelResolution1b_013=reeled once before crumpling to the mossy ground. The bullet had hit a major artery that could not be sutured before the loss of blood overwhelmed them. On the more matter-of-fact side, the body that remained was otherwise untouched and was returned to the estate within hours.
DuelResolution1b_014=disappeared into a swirling silver vortex, leaving behind only a single hand that attempted to prevent this occurrence by grabbing onto a nearby metal fixture. It wriggled for a few moments before expiring.
DuelResolution1b_015=was unceremoniously crushed between two bronze gears. The machine created for this event would need to be disassembled and cleaned before it could be used again.
DuelResolution1b_016=withered into a rubbery scrap of skin, their blood having been accidentally distilled during the duel. Thankfully, the beakers and pipettes involved in the process could still be used after a proper scrubbing.
DuelResolution1b_017=was mauled and desecrated into an unrecognizable pile of exposed flesh and muscle. Appreciatively, the experiment used in the duel was docile after feeding and easily recaptured.
DuelResolution1b_018=As blood pooled beneath them, staining the dueling grounds crimson, I shielded my eyes and fled from the site. The duel had ended in death. The generation would have to continue based solely upon their willed instructions, penned weeks before the lethal event. 
DuelResolution1b_019={duelloser} must place their **Self** into Lost. This piece cannot be reclaimed for the remainder of this Generation. 
DuelResolution1b_020={duelloser} gains their Caretaker piece from Lost (if possible). _As outlined in their will, in order to execute actions posthumously in case of their untimely demise._
DuelResolution1b_021=Also, {duelloser} gains a {icon:bodies_icon}.

# passages/00185-AdvancedWeaponryIntro.mws.yaml
AdvancedWeaponryIntro_001=A Few Improvements
AdvancedWeaponryIntro_002=I was quick to suggest a few "enhancements" to their battery and presented several **advanced weaponry** schematics which could prove instrumental to victory.
AdvancedWeaponryIntro_003=While the rumors of my parent's eccentricities made them hesitant, the promise of support from my lucrative estate proved too much to resist. If I could demonstrate to them the visceral efficacy of my proposal, they promised further investment. An easy task.
AdvancedWeaponryIntro_004=Retrieve the **Advanced Weaponry** Experiment cards. Shuffle these cards and place them face-down nearby to form their own deck.
AdvancedWeaponryIntro_005=Each player then draws an **Advanced Weaponry** card.
AdvancedWeaponryIntro_006=you may gain 1 Servant from Lost and lose 1 {icon:creepy_icon} .
AdvancedWeaponryIntro_007=you may gain 1 Servant from Lost and gain 1VP.
AdvancedWeaponryIntro_008=you may gain 1 Servant from Lost and 1 Knowledge of your choice.
AdvancedWeaponryIntro_009=you may pay $1 to gain 1 Caretaker from Lost.
AdvancedWeaponryIntro_010=you may gain 1 Caretaker from Lost.
AdvancedWeaponryIntro_011=you may gain 1 Knowledge of your choice and 1VP.
AdvancedWeaponryIntro_012=no bonus.
AdvancedWeaponryIntro_013=$1 for your efforts.

# passages/00186-TakeEventb.mws.yaml
TakeEventb_001=Votes Tallied
TakeEventb_002=Tally the vote count _(ties are broken by the player who went last during the Middle Years)_.
TakeEventb_004=Yay. We voted to build a Barracks.
TakeEventb_005=Nay. We voted ''against''.

# passages/00187-TakeEventFlag.mws.yaml
TakeEventFlag_001=Change of Allegiance
TakeEventFlag_002=A new flag had been raised at the Town Hall. It was nice to see the town finally listening to reason. Certainly a triumph, but I had no delusions that their attitude towards my ingenious inventions had suddenly transformed.
TakeEventFlag_003=This small change was only the beginning. Before long they would tremble as I wielded the awesome power of science!
TakeEventFlag_004=Return the {warloser} Flag card to the Scenario box. Place the {warwinner} Flag card face-up near the Village Chronicle.

# passages/00188-TTBarracksPenalty.mws.yaml
TTBarracksPenalty_001=Barracks Penalty
TTBarracksPenalty_002=Any player that does **not** have a piece of their color on the Barracks must **lose 5VP**.

# passages/00189-TSBarracksPenalty.mws.yaml
TSBarracksPenalty_001=Lack of Service Penalty
TSBarracksPenalty_002=If any player's Caretaker remains on the Barracks at the End of the Generation, they immediately **lose 5VP**.

# passages/00190-TowardsDev.mws.yaml
TowardsDev_001=Under Unfortunate Circumstances
TowardsDev_002=Perform the End of the Generation as normal, but do **NOT** discard your completed Experiments. Remove all player pieces from the board. Return any unused {icon:s3_sickletoken} , {icon:s3_shieldtoken} , and {icon:s3_woodenfiguretoken} tokens to the Scenario box.
TowardsDev_003=Today, I write these words in a feeble hand under grievous conditions from a location which I dare not reveal. The circumstances of my departure from my estate will become all too apparent to my next of kin. To be relegated to exile in my final days is a fate I never would have foreseen. 
TowardsDev_004=Without the support of the Barracks, the {warwinner} were unable to protect the strategically important village from being collateral damage on the frontlines of battle.
TowardsDev_005=Unfortunately, the {warwinner} Barracks became a central target of the war effort. While the {warwinner} was able to hold the position, they could not prevent the village from becoming collateral damage on the frontlines of battle.
TowardsDev_006=But even with my final breath, I am stalwart in my hope that my latest discovery will ensure these very words will be prized by future generations. I am, as ever, a servant to science.

# passages/00191-TMReplace.mws.yaml
TMReplace_001=A Time Loop Created
TMReplace_002=I remember thoughts racing within my mind just as the essence of time spiraled around this grand machine. Could this be the awesome, final form of the Masterwork which my grandfather had entrusted to my lineage? And if so, was I destined to be successful in creating this contraption?
TMReplace_003=Retrieve the **Time Machine** Update card from the Scenario box and give it to the player working towards this Masterwork.

# passages/00192-ParadoxExReminder.mws.yaml
ParadoxExReminder_001=Removing Paradox
ParadoxExReminder_002=Experiments that have Paradox tokens {icon:s3_paradoxtoken} are considered incomplete Experiments. When you **Perform an Experiment**, you may instead complete an Experiment with a {icon:s3_paradoxtoken} token in your play area as if it were played from your hand. 
ParadoxExReminder_003=Pay all applicable costs, return the {icon:s3_paradoxtoken} token to the Scenario box, and receive **all rewards as normal**. The completed Experiment remains face-up in front of you and counts as the type (A, B, or C) listed.
ParadoxExReminder_004= _tokens are meant to be infinite. In the rare case that you do not have enough tokens, use another marker as a substitute until there are enough remaining._

# passages/00193-ATimeMachineRepaired.mws.yaml
ATimeMachineRepaired_001=A Vehicle Through Time
ATimeMachineRepaired_002=Returned to its former magnificence, the small metal room shook the dust from its old dials. Polished brass fixtures, steel riveting, a fresh coat of lead indigo paint, and complex gold lines on thin petroleum-based resin to carry the electrical currents with infernal precision; it was a masterpiece from a future that could only be possible through my legacy.
ATimeMachineRepaired_003=The time machine was complete. And though I knew there was still work to be done to repair the timestream, I would return soon to pilot it.

# passages/00194-TimeEnd2b.mws.yaml
TimeEnd2b_001=An Unsettling Time
TimeEnd2b_002=Through some stroke of luck and some hasty tinkering, the rusted box sparked its way to life, sputtering in protest the entire time. With {tmnumber} polished and fastened into place I was convinced that this endeavor would prove fruitful.
TimeEnd2b_003=It took another full year for me to build the stamina to attempt the journey, but with cane in hand, I secured the chamber door and pulled the lever.
TimeEnd2b_004=Surely, this would work.
TimeEnd2b_005=Through some stroke of luck and some hasty tinkering, the rusted box sparked its way to life, sputtering in protest the entire time. The strangled noises it made did not bode well for a smooth adventure through time.
TimeEnd2b_006=Well, shit. I don't have much to lose at this point. Might as well pull the lever and see what happens!

# passages/00195-Late2ResA.mws.yaml
Late2ResA_002=For a reason which was never fully explained to me - I assumed it was my family's influence on events long past - the villagers were even more jovial and accepting of me continuing the important work left to gather dust for so many years. They even opened their coffers to me.
Late2ResA_003=It would have been uncouth of me not to accept their generosity despite, and I assure you of this fact, my considerable wealth.
Late2ResA_004=Each player gains 2 Resources (of any type) from the supply and adds them to their Quarters.

# passages/00196-Late2ResB.mws.yaml
Late2ResB_001=For some reason which was never fully explained to me - I assumed it was my family's willingness to **fully and silently collaborate** in the past - the villagers were even more jovial and accepting of me continuing the important work left to gather dust for so many years. They even opened their coffers to me.
Late2ResB_002=It would have been uncouth of me not to accept their generosity despite, and I assure you of this fact, my considerable and self-made wealth.
Late2ResB_003=Each player **gains 2 Resources (of any type)** from the supply and adds them to their Quarters.

# passages/00197-WhoopsUtopian.mws.yaml
WhoopsUtopian_001=The Future is NOW
WhoopsUtopian_002=While the journal of my parents was an astonishing discovery in itself, I did not realize that the true revelation would arrive several weeks later when I rifled through the pages willed to me. I suspect that you may assume that my memory had slipped or that I had not been thorough in my studies of those browning pages locked within the cellar laboratory, but I swear by my blood to be true.
WhoopsUtopian_003=I had read over the myriad notes and journal entries so many times that I had memorized their contents, yet one afternoon when I turned to a central page, several pristine and folded pieces of parchment fell to the floor. A faint and acrid scent of burnt oil wafted from the papers, which each detailed a new, amazing schematic for devices far more advanced than any I had ever perceived possible.
WhoopsUtopian_004=Return the **Time Machine Repairs** cards to the Scenario box.
WhoopsUtopian_005=Retrieve the **Utopian Experiments** from the box. Shuffle them face-down and place them nearby to form a deck. 

# passages/00198-FigureontheTrackIn.mws.yaml
FigureontheTrackIn_001=**Carefully hand this Storybook device to the player with the {figure} token and do not allow any other players to see the screen.**
FigureontheTrackIn_002=**Nostalgic Guests**
FigureontheTrackIn_003=I wasn't quite sure why the mantle in my study was adorned with a small metal {figure}. As with much of the decor, I allowed my spouse free reign over matters of interior decoration, and thought nothing of it until a dinner guest became enamored with its presence.
FigureontheTrackIn_004=He doffed his top hat and brass monocle to put the object to closer inspection. "I thought they had all been destroyed after the war so many years ago. Curious that you would proudly display such a vulgar symbol of aggression!"
FigureontheTrackIn_005=Little did I realize the rumors I would soon endure from this singular supper event.
FigureontheTrackIn_006=Gain 2 {icon:creepy_icon}.

# passages/00199-FigureontheTrackInb.mws.yaml
FigureontheTrackInb_001=A Legacy of Intrigue
FigureontheTrackInb_002=The {figure} I so obliviously kept upon my mantle became a topic of conversation around town, becoming a central source of intrigue for my secret work. They began to ask me questions, even as I became more bold and curt with my responses. 
FigureontheTrackInb_003=However, I soon discovered that their sneers weren't sneers of derision, merely appropriate disgust at the necessary but sometimes graphic lengths to which my experimentation perched upon the bleeding edge of innovation. To my surprise, as I began to hold a grotesque exhibition of some of my family's preserved works, the academic response was one of motivation.
FigureontheTrackInb_004=Although I could not withhold my vocal disdain for extrinsic motivations - wretched carrots dangled tenuously in front of weaker minds - I also recognized that if I could cause them to react in a fervor, I could expect rapturous applause instead of pitchforks. However, it would take significant effort to do so.
FigureontheTrackInb_005=Remove the Suspicion Marker and {icon:angrymob_icon} Marker from the {icon:creepy_icon} Track. The player with the {figure} token places it on space **{accolade}** of the {icon:creepy_icon} Track.

# passages/00200-MonumentVote.mws.yaml
MonumentVote_001=Time Machine
MonumentVote_002=Publication?
MonumentVote_003=While the ideas set forth in my parent's journal entries were both outdated and embarrassingly rudimentary in some areas, one thing that the fools in academia hounded us to provide was the schematics to the Time Conveyance Device. For a discovery so radical and immense in its influence on multiple dimensions of the world, the meager sums they offered for entrusting it to their universities was insulting.
MonumentVote_004=I would never give it to them to abuse secretly at their discretion. No! But to publish it widely and allow all of the Hungarian people the chance to rewrite history? That, it seemed, would be the sort of experimental chaos the stuffed shirts at the university would never see coming!
MonumentVote_005=But, perhaps, and most undoubtably, it would have untold repercussions.
MonumentVote_006=The issue at hand, however, was the matter of secrecy. If any one of us - myself or my dear cousins - decided to publish the schematic, it would be freely available.
MonumentVote_007=I knew that each would need to make their own private decision and I prayed that it would be the correct choice.

# passages/00201-NobodyFigures.mws.yaml
NobodyFigures_001=Accolades for Exploration
NobodyFigures_002=I soon discovered that the sneers I sometimes received when I offered hints of my secret work weren't sneers of derision, merely appropriate disgust at the necessary, but sometimes graphic lengths to which my experimentation perched upon the bleeding edge of innovation. To my surprise, as I began to hold a grotesque exhibition of some of my family's preserved works, the academic response was one of motivation.
NobodyFigures_003=While the masses could never fully appreciate the breadth of study required in order to create such exquisite revelations, I could see no reason to invite their animosity. When the townsfolk began to offer assistance as my work teetered on the brink of ethicality, I vowed to press onward further than ever before and embrace the fervor that would surround it.
NobodyFigures_004=Remove the Suspicion Marker and {icon:angrymob_icon} Marker from the {icon:creepy_icon} Track. Retrieve the {figure} token and place it on space **{accolade}** of the {icon:creepy_icon} Track.

# passages/00202-SecretParadoxBonus.mws.yaml
SecretParadoxBonus_001=Chaos Theory
SecretParadoxBonus_002=Sometimes, resistance carried with it hidden rewards. By studying the effects of rifts in time, I unlocked a new understanding of fourth-dimensional forces that others would never dare to discover. Only the boldest and brightest flames survive the winds of chaos, and I would blaze forward until my last breath!
SecretParadoxBonus_003=The player(s) with the most {icon:s3_paradoxtoken} tokens remaining on their Experiments gains **4VP** and may immediately advance their lowest Journal Track 1 space at no cost (_if multiple tracks are lowest, they may choose_).
SecretParadoxBonus_004=You must have at least 1 {icon:s3_paradoxtoken} token to gain this bonus.

# passages/00203-WarningWarEnding.mws.yaml
WarningWarEnding_001=The War?
WarningWarEnding_002=As a brief consideration for those who may read these words and perceive a gap in the narrative of my family's lineage, I will address the period of civil war that was mentioned so often a full generation previous. 
WarningWarEnding_003=Though details about this minor conflict are sparse, I could discern that 
WarningWarEnding_004=the {warwinner} were able to quash the minor events of the 1860's and 70's, easing minor taxation grievances and relegating this civil war to a few muckraking, sensationalist headlines in the emerging newspapers.
WarningWarEnding_005=In fact, it was so difficult to find materials related to the disagreement that I could not understand my family's fascination with the events. Suffice to say, it had minimal effects on my current affairs.
WarningWarEnding_006=the {warwinner} were able to use public pressure to establish a republican house with only minor skirmishes and rebellions along the way. Working in tandem with a figurehead monarchy, a democratic process was enacted.
WarningWarEnding_007=Decidedly trivial and woefully boring, I could not understand my family's fascination with the events. Suffice to say, it had minimal effects on my current state.

# passages/00204-WarningMaybe.mws.yaml
WarningMaybe_001=One Last Opportunity
WarningMaybe_002=In the weeks previous, I had felt a strange premonition. As was sometimes the case when an inquisitive townsperson visited the grounds or a courier who delivered a sensitive parcel to my door in the evening became too friendly, I would hastily conceal my workspace and destroy anything that revealed too much. But, this was... different.
WarningMaybe_003=Things were about to change and I would not be left witless and unable to progress further in my work.
WarningMaybe_004=**WARNING: You will not be able to gain new Advanced Ingredients until the timeline is restored.** _This may never happen._
WarningMaybe_005=Each player may decide to discard any Utopian Experiments from their hand. For each Experiment discarded, you may draw 1 Experiment to replace it from the deck of your choice.

# passages/00205-AcceptDuel1b.mws.yaml
AcceptDuel1b_001=Duel Accepted
AcceptDuel1b_002=Though I perceived my body as merely a vessel to contain my brilliant mind and dreaded to imagine the wasted time it would take to martial my skills, I would nevertheless answer in the affirmative. Under the eyes of God and the Devil, I would strike with precision and settle this matter with spilt blood.
AcceptDuel1b_003=I decided that honor was above all. I would not be bullied into submission by a sycophant searching for recognition. If a duel was required, then a duel we shall have!

# passages/00206-ATOWSabotageIntro2.mws.yaml
ATOWSabotageIntro2_002=It was time to strike while my passions were still agitated! But, was it in my best interest to turn my destructive gaze towards the {warloser}'s noble cause? Or perhaps one of my kin could stand to be targeted by my ire?

# passages/00207-SabotagePlayerChoice1.mws.yaml
SabotagePlayerChoice1_001=The Target of My Wrath
SabotagePlayerChoice1_002=My grim sabotage was swift and well-orchestrated. Perhaps my family would reconsider their apathy towards me after witnessing the utter devastation I could cause to their reputations.
SabotagePlayerChoice1_003=After one fateful evening, I knew that they would **lose 3VP** & could possibly have to destroy a completed Experiment.
SabotagePlayerChoice1_004=**Please click on the name of the player you would like to sabotage:**
SabotagePlayerChoice1_005=Or I could still decide to 
SabotagePlayerChoice1_006=click here and let bygones be bygones.

# passages/00208-SabotageSignIn1.mws.yaml
SabotageSignIn1_001=Making it Personal
SabotageSignIn1_002=I could no longer turn a blind eye to their meddling. Like the clanging chime of a brass bell on a longcase clock, the time had come for an insidious misfortune to befall one of my dear cousins. 

# passages/00209-ATOWSabotageNO.mws.yaml
ATOWSabotageNO_001=Avoid Indulgence
ATOWSabotageNO_002=Study was essential! Alas, I could not allow myself idle time to indulge in immediate self-gratification. To attack one's own rivals was in itself admitting that they were, in fact, valid competition. In reality, my contributions would far exceed their meager offerings.
ATOWSabotageNO_003=There was no need for pomp and explosions. I was a true craftsman dedicated to the art of science. My focus was indomitable and this dedication would see me victorious!
ATOWSabotageNO_004=Gain **1 Knowledge cube of your choice**.
ATOWSabotageNO_005=Gain **1 Compulsion**.

# passages/00210-ATOWSabotageIntro2Sep.mws.yaml
ATOWSabotageIntro2Sep_001=While I had seen what devastation was wrought first-hand by the cruelty of sabotage, this knowledge only made my sense of justice more clear.
ATOWSabotageIntro2Sep_002=It was the time to strike while my passions were still agitated! But, was it in my best interest to turn my destructive gaze towards the {warloser}'s noble cause and crush the Outpost at the edge of town? Or perhaps one of my kin should be targeted by my ire?
ATOWSabotageIntro2Sep_003=I chose to sabotage the ''Outpost''.

# passages/00213-Sabotage1Now.mws.yaml
Sabotage1Now_001=Cruel Betrayal
Sabotage1Now_002=The exterior wall near the corner of my estate had been struck by an explosive device. I was immediately suspicious of the clear lines of soot at the base, suggesting that the demolition had in fact been calculated to expose a portion of my laboratory.
Sabotage1Now_003=The papers within my laboratory were scattered about and a small fire had claimed and blackened a portion of the room. Given the frequency of loud noises and odoriferous ingredients emanating from the room, I was not surprised when none in the house noticed anything amiss.
Sabotage1Now_004=I awoke to discover a section of my estate in shambles! {_rnd_Sabotage1Now_0}
Sabotage1Now_005=Though the repairs would prove arduous, it would not deter me from my work. If others were so wanton or jealous as to try to destroy what I had created, it was clear that my work was more vital than ever before!
Sabotage1Now_006=and must **discard 1 Experiment** they completed this Generation.
Sabotage1Now_007={sabotagee1} **loses 3VP**{_rnd_Sabotage1Now_0}

# passages/00214-SabotagePlayerConfirmed.mws.yaml
SabotagePlayerConfirmed_001=The Choice Was Made
SabotagePlayerConfirmed_002={sabotagee1} would shoulder the burden for the misery they had caused me. 

# passages/00215-DuelResolution1sci.mws.yaml
DuelResolution1sci_001=Science
DuelResolution1sci_002=Please choose which player had the highest scientific prowess in {duelsci}:
DuelResolution1sci_003={sabotagee1} had the most.
