# passages/00216-ScienceDuelTiedRes.mws.yaml
ScienceDuelTiedRes_001=Stalemate
ScienceDuelTiedRes_002=I was quite unimpressed by the efforts of my family member, but while it vexed me to admit it, I was ultimately unable to crush their pitiful {duelsci} exploits with my own. We did not speak nor shake hands as we exited the dueling grounds, resentment simmering in our heads.
ScienceDuelTiedRes_003={sabotagee1} and {playersabotage1} both **gain 1** {icon:creepy_icon}.

# passages/00217-MartialSepEventb.mws.yaml
MartialSepEventb_001=Total Bribe
MartialSepEventb_002=Tally the amount of money that all players have revealed.
MartialSepEventb_003=**Was the bribe amount equal to or greater than the ${milit} needed to sway their opinion?**
MartialSepEventb_004=Yes!

# passages/00218-MartialSepEventYes.mws.yaml
MartialSepEventYes_001=Success
MartialSepEventYes_002=I regret to say that perserverance alone does not advance one's goals in the hills of Bohemia. A small investment and showmanship to back it up, now that's what impresses a red-blooded Austro-Hungarian. Especially when one can view so much of that warm blood festooning the battlefield with such dazzling radiance!
MartialSepEventYes_003=It is this showmanship, and the strategic concealment of it when negotiations are being penned, that will advance the Hungarian conflict to a swift conclusion.
MartialSepEventYes_004=The player that offered the **most** money also gains **3VP**. _If there is a tie, all tied players gain this bonus._
MartialSepEventYes_005=Then, all players with money in their fists pay that money to the supply.

# passages/00219-MartialSepEventNo.mws.yaml
MartialSepEventNo_001=Failure
MartialSepEventNo_002=My experiments are not some frivolous diversion for the gossipmongers of {townname} to mock as they please! They looked at me as if I were intending to replace the gears in my longcase clock with stock and barrel of a rifle. Are we not creating weapons of war? Why would compounding weaponry with additional weaponry be unnacceptable?
MartialSepEventNo_003=I could not imagine a more advantageous arrangement. However, if the military establishment has no need for the innovation I would bring to the table, then I will put my services to better use!
MartialSepEventNo_004=Any player that offered at least $1 towards the bribe, **draws 1 Compulsion**. 
MartialSepEventNo_005=Then, all players return their money to their Quarters.

# passages/00220-BribeDenied.mws.yaml
BribeDenied_001=Royal Disinterest
BribeDenied_002=With the royalty expressing less interest in our experimentations, the use of weaponry to aid in the performing of experiments had lost its luster with the passing generation. I perceived this not as a stumbling block, but as an opportunity. Focusing purely on weapons had made my parent's remaining exhibits dull and one-note.
BribeDenied_003=I, however, would forge a new path. One that would no longer rely on the crutch of warring factions, but would inspire future generations with its innovation!
BribeDenied_004=**Players are no longer able to substitute a {icon:s3_weapontoken} token for an Ingredient.**

# passages/00221-OutpostExplain.mws.yaml
OutpostExplain_001=OUTPOST
OutpostExplain_002=When you visit the Outpost, you may pay {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens to acquire Resources and special actions. With each visit you may perform **as many trades as you like**:
OutpostExplain_003=Pay 2 {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens to **gain $1.**
OutpostExplain_004=Pay 3 {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens to **gain a Knowledge cube of your choice.**
OutpostExplain_005=Pay 4 {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens to **Lose 1** {icon:creepy_icon}**.**

# passages/00222-PotentBuyBonus.mws.yaml
PotentBuyBonus_001=Significant Investment

# passages/00223-ResistEnd3.mws.yaml
ResistEnd3_001=Shots Fired
ResistEnd3_002=It appeared that the contributions of my cousins and I - as entirely expected - were the deciding factor in the war effort for the {warloser}. Our advanced, modern weaponry had proven essential on the battlefield and truly captured the hearts and minds of the populace. But would it be enough? 
ResistEnd3_003=**Count the number of completed Advanced Weaponry Experiments among all players.** If this number is equal to or greater than **{defense}**, then the {warloser} were successful in overtaking the town's defenses. Otherwise, the {warwinner} have won the war.
ResistEnd3_004=Click here if the {warloser} were successful
ResistEnd3_005=Click here if the {warwinner} defended the attack and won the war.

# passages/00224-ParadoxRandoEvent.mws.yaml
ParadoxRandoEvent_001=The Consequences of Free Time Travel
ParadoxRandoEvent_002=The fools! The absolute imbeciles! The diabolical currs! My cousins knew there could be dire consequences for allowing time travel to become accessible to almost anyone, and now I would be forced to abide the random effects of a force unknown. 
ParadoxRandoEvent_003=Click to create a new paradox!

# passages/00225-TimeTravelEventb.mws.yaml
TimeTravelEventb_002=These schematics weren't exactly what I had envisioned as a chilling and ethically dubious leap into the future of science, but they were certainly handy around the house.
TimeTravelEventb_003=If one could procure the additional materials required to create them, I was convinced that these devious advanced devices would allow me to achieve the proper recognition I deserved.

