# passages/00237-ATOW-FamineEventYes.mws.yaml
ATOW_FamineEventYes_001=A Modest Proposal
ATOW_FamineEventYes_002=Carefully pass the Storybook to the player who won the bid. Please enter the name of the new meat product:
ATOW_FamineEventYes_003=The riots ceased and a calm set in across the valley. With an influx of fresh, surprisingly tender cuts of **{newmeat}** and the introduction of salted, canned **{newmeat}** rations, the effort at home and abroad was bolstered immeasurably. Faced with the prospect of starvation, it was startling how readily individuals would not question how a famine could provide such a bounteous wintry season. 
ATOW_FamineEventYes_004=All players **gain 2** {icon:insanity_icon}. 

# passages/00238-ATOW-FamineEventNo.mws.yaml
ATOW_FamineEventNo_001=Hardened by Suffering
ATOW_FamineEventNo_002=The citizenry rebelled throughout the region after another year of rationing left thousands to wither away when the cold season swept through the mountains. Our decision carried with it enough clout that the populace were aware of our impotence, and they most certainly held a grudge which made visits to town much less amenable.
ATOW_FamineEventNo_003=Move the {icon:angrymob_icon} Marker 2 spaces to the left.

# passages/00239-PeaceWar.mws.yaml
PeaceWar_001=The War to End All Wars
PeaceWar_002=With my inventions (and regrettably those of my close cousins) spearheading the warfront, I was suitably convinced of swift victory and the capitulation of nearby nations to our unprecedented technological might. However, I was less convinced that the president and the generals he commanded would properly assign credit for the advantageous position which I provided.
PeaceWar_003=My own family vied for the same notoriety and with each major conflict interceded with their own unjust claims for recognition. Rightfully so, I was unable to share these accolades with those who offered such lesser contributions.
PeaceWar_004=Retrieve the **World Conquest** card and place it **World Conquest** side up. 
PeaceWar_005=For 2 players, cover the bottom-most square on the World Conquest card with a {icon:bodies_icon} Resource. You will not resolve this battle on this card.
PeaceWar_006=For 3 players, cover the top-most square on the World Conquest card with a {icon:bodies_icon} Resource. You will not resolve this battle on this card.
PeaceWar_007=Place an Occult cube onto the highest square.

# passages/00240-PeaceDiscard.mws.yaml
PeaceDiscard_001=Degradation Over Time
PeaceDiscard_002=I was agitated by the intrusion of politics into my affairs and inevitably by the toll time had taken on my family's reputation. At least the additional contributions of previous generations was not entirely without merit. My family's lasting impact increased my renown significantly.
PeaceDiscard_003=Any player who has more than **{wlimit}** {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens must discard tokens until they have {wlimit} in total. For each discarded token, that player **gains 1VP**.

# passages/00241-PeacePrep.mws.yaml
PeacePrep_001=In Preparation
PeacePrep_002=I knew that to claim eternal infamy for conquest of the globe would require more preparation than ever before. And so I spent countless evenings developing novel and aggressive peace-keeping measures that would inspire awe for years to come. This was a rare opportunity for my most cataclysmic and exhilarating experiments to be unleashed upon a vast testing field, and I would seize it!
PeacePrep_003=Each player draws **1 Advanced Weaponry** Experiment card.
PeacePrep_004=Each player collects **2** {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens.

# passages/00242-PeacetoRebuild.mws.yaml
PeacetoRebuild_001=The Price of Peace
PeacetoRebuild_002=The wounds of the recent civil war were still raw and the process of rebuilding was not an inexpensive proposition. While I pledged to offer assistance in any way that my humble, self-driven, well-educated mind could, I was quite surprised when they actually had the indecency to act upon this proposal.
PeacetoRebuild_003=The Separatist government enforced 
PeacetoRebuild_004=a recurring estate tax of $1 - to rebuild several buildings - that would go into effect consistently _(at the start of each new round)_. While at least it would not rob me of my most precious resource - time - it would sour my mood upon days of leisure.
PeacetoRebuild_005=no new taxes, thankfully, as zero buildings were sabotaged in the previous generation. At least consistent support for my native country had its benefits.
PeacetoRebuild_006=a one-time estate inheritance tax of $1 - due to a single building being destroyed - which would go into effect during my early years. While at least it would not rob me of my most precious resource - time - it would sour my mood upon days of leisure.

# passages/00243-FinalBattleComplete.mws.yaml
FinalBattleComplete_001=Campaign Complete
FinalBattleComplete_002=The player with the most remaining {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens gains a Vanity Estate Upgrade of their choice. _If there is a tie, all tied players choose and gain an Upgrade in turn order._
FinalBattleComplete_003=You must still pay the cost to expand your Estate if needed.
FinalBattleComplete_004=Any players with unused {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens must now discard them to the Scenario box. **For every 2** {icon:s3_weapontoken} **tokens** returned this way, that player **gains 1VP**.
FinalBattleComplete_005=Click to move to Final Scoring...

# passages/00244-ShadowBonus.mws.yaml
ShadowBonus_001=Royal Advisor
ShadowBonus_002=The player(s) closest to the {icon:s3_crowntoken} token on the {icon:creepy_icon} Track without overlapping or exceeding it **gains 6VP**. _All tied players receive the full VP amount._
ShadowBonus_003=Multiple players are tied, so no player

# passages/00245-CrownCons.mws.yaml
CrownCons_001=Royal Suspicions
CrownCons_002=Now that the crown's notice had fallen upon us, the penalty was not as dire, but still carried with it permanent consequences. With the lamplight shone upon my work, what I could once stash away in the shadows now was laid bare.
CrownCons_003=The player who triggered this event removes their {icon:creepy_icon} Marker from the {icon:creepy_icon} Track and places it on top of their Score Track Marker.

# passages/00246-COWRes.mws.yaml
COWRes_002=Tally the vote count _(if there is a tie, the outcome is_ **benevolence**_)_.
COWRes_003=We chose to rule with benevolence. (Yay!)
COWRes_005=We chose to rule with an iron fist. (Nay!)

# passages/00247-PeaceEventb.mws.yaml
PeaceEventb_001=Live or Die
PeaceEventb_002=In turn order, each player raises their right hand. Holding it outstretched, they either raise their thumb skyward or point it to the Earth. A **thumbs down** is a vote to release the gas.
PeaceEventb_003=A vote to **release the gas** will pacify the people and impress the leadership – though they will be suspicious – but at what cost?
PeaceEventb_004=A vote against will also pacify the people, but provides no other benefit.
PeaceEventb_005=_(Ties are broken by the player last in turn order this round.)_

# passages/00248-PeaceStick.mws.yaml
PeaceStick_001=An Old, Failed Sabotage
PeaceStick_002=For as long as I could remember, the dusty, misshapen thing sat perched upon the bookshelf. However, it wasn't until I needed an old textbook behind it, that I finally inspected the object thoroughly.
PeaceStick_003=I discovered a thin circular cut in the top portion of the formless wooden carving. Upon tapping it on the edge of a table, the cut revealed what looked like a stopper and the remains of an old adhesive. With one more solid whack, I stumbled backwards and shielded my eyes as a cloud of black powder burst from the interior. A blasting cap?
PeaceStick_004=Why some individual would plant an explosive device in a crudely whittled container is beyond my understanding! It was too ancient, of course, to actually cause harm, however, I was able to salvage the well-preserved gunpowder for future use.
PeaceStick_005=Each player with a {icon:s3_woodenfiguretoken} token gains 1 {icon:s3_weapontoken} token. 
PeaceStick_006=The player with the {icon:s3_woodenfiguretoken} token gains 2 {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens. 
PeaceStick_007=Then, discard the tokens to the Scenario box. 

# passages/00249-ATOW-FamineEventRes.mws.yaml
ATOW_FamineEventRes_001=**Tally the vote count.** _(Ties are broken by the player who went last during the Early Years)_

# passages/00250-ATOW-FamineEventV.mws.yaml
ATOW_FamineEventV_002=Each player takes a Voting token into their fist and secretly chooses a side. When all players have chosen, simultaneously reveal your vote.
ATOW_FamineEventV_003=**YAY** is a vote to create a new meat product. (The people will be pacified, but at what cost?)
ATOW_FamineEventV_004=**NAY** is a vote to weather the storm. (The people will be **angry**.)
ATOW_FamineEventV_005=Tally the vote count _(ties are broken by the player who went last during the Early Years)._

# passages/00251-ATOW-End1.mws.yaml
ATOW_End1_001=A Giant Success
ATOW_End1_002=And so it is that this chapter of the story has concluded. It is a story that you no doubt have read about countless times in the newspapers or heard with your family while in the sitting room huddled around your radioscope. The **immensity** of my family's experiment astounds even myself as I crane my neck to look upon it in all its magnificence.
ATOW_End1_003=But damn it all, I swear on my name, {winner} IV, that I will use this bit of fame to fuel my ambitions to the stars. Reaching Utopia is not enough; I must aim higher.
ATOW_End1_004=Releasing the Time Machine schematics had surprisingly little effect, or possibly it had an infinite number of consequences, which technically amounts to no effect at all. And if it did have an effect, I would certainly have no knowledge of the effect's effect as the timeline would have already twisted my knowledge of it. Suffice to say, with time travel, as with real life, everything and nothing matters.
ATOW_End1_005=Giant Spider Chariot
ATOW_End1_006=Giant Love Potion
ATOW_End1_007=Giant Teleportation Device
ATOW_End1_008=What could be more innovative than a Giant Time Machine or a {_rnd_ATOW_End1_0}, you wonder? Why an even BIGGER version, of course! One of tremendous size!
ATOW_End1_009=This is not the end; it is only the beginning. My own story still remains to be written, forged into legacy like those before me. I will not stop until the sun is blotted out by the sheer heftiness of my imagination!

# passages/00252-ATOW-End2.mws.yaml
ATOW_End2_001=Behind the Curve
ATOW_End2_002=My close friends and family - many of whom I have permanently severed contact with because of their feelings on the matter - have expressed extreme misgivings about the publication of this book. They claim that my macabre fascination with exposing this to the world is unhealthy! 
ATOW_End2_003=Some have even derisively labeled this work as pseudoscience, homeopathy, or a drug-induced fever dream, but I say to them, "who are you to criticize the moon and the stars for being in the sky?" This work is important! How can they not see it? If anything, these outlandish experiments further prove the relevance of the science that is far better researched, performed, and peer-reviewed after publication in respected journals. 
ATOW_End2_004=For while the world may have sped onward at a pace that our scientific contributions could not match, rendering our innovations lame and timid in comparison, I believe that my family's failure to make an impact on a world of the future is an important lesson. Our contributions must be remembered, not for their value to the progress of mankind, but for laying the foundations of the work that others would ignore because of other more viable innovations which they could hone to perfection.
ATOW_End2_005=The world may have progressed beyond a need for mad science, but I believe it is this spirit that will define my family's legacy. Even if what they did, does not.

# passages/00253-ATOW-End3.mws.yaml
ATOW_End3_001=A Wrinkle Within Time
ATOW_End3_002=The astute reader may have already surmised that the recollections of three generations was at many points noticeably vivid and detailed. Almost as if the author were not simply transcribing those moments from memory, but witnessing them first-hand. If not, then perhaps I am not as adept at my writing craft as I give myself credit. 
ATOW_End3_003=Does it not seem peculiar that an individual from {townname}, a small town in Eastern Europe, would become a household name at such a pace? Quite peculiar indeed, isn't it?
ATOW_End3_004=For you see, it was I, {winner}, editor, author, and compiler of my family's illustrious personal memoir. This was not a memoir as proposed, but a non-fiction chronicle of events witnessed directly by myself. Being gifted a schematic of a Time Machine certainly has its benefits. 
ATOW_End3_005=I will not attempt to persuade you to the authenticity of my account. With all the wondrous occurrences and graphic failures described within this lengthy tome - that I'm sure my family would never have admitted to of their own volition - I have no doubt that this revelation carries with it more credibility.
ATOW_End3_006=With the timeline repaired, I feel compelled to offer this history as a testament to the industrious lineage to which I am indebted and to cement their achievements into the firmament of scientific history forever.

# passages/00254-ATOW-End4.mws.yaml
ATOW_End4_001=A Timeline Unbound
ATOW_End4_002=The words scatter and reform as I move my pen about the page. Like rusted leaves turned to beetles, they skitter towards the margins. The ink flows to the nub and surges back inside. The twine that binds the pages, the glue that grips the spine, bound and unbound again, it all flits by reality like a zoopraxiscope, projected images of distorted timelines with minor changes.
ATOW_End4_003=I cannot know if this memoir is complete. I cannot know if anyone will see these words. The veins on my fingers change color. The {warwinner} won the war. I cannot tell if I am real or a projection. The twine that binds the pages, the glue that grips the spine... Am I repeating myself?
ATOW_End4_004=Can you read this?
ATOW_End4_005=Can you read these words?
ATOW_End4_006=Is there no response? Who do I presume would respond but myself?
ATOW_End4_007=I cannot know if anyone will see these words. Like rusted beetles, leaves that skitter margins unbound
ATOW_End4_008=Can you page the about pen my move I as reform and scatter words the 

# passages/00255-ATOW-End5.mws.yaml
ATOW_End5_001=Royal Praise
ATOW_End5_002=After the passing of my beloved parents, who were never able to see what their influence had accomplished, I was able to compile this extended memoir which I have no doubt will be received equitably with my abridgements.
ATOW_End5_003=The royalty were pleased with the successes brought about in part by my family. They appreciated the tenacity displayed when they 
ATOW_End5_004=were against the move to establish a costly barracks in a region when the prevailing opinions were so strong.
ATOW_End5_005=could not in good conscience create a barracks for the wrong side of the conflict.
ATOW_End5_006=supported the building of a barracks for the royal government.
ATOW_End5_007=supported the establishment of an initial barracks and armed stronghold within the region.
ATOW_End5_008=They remained loyal from generation to generation and helped 
ATOW_End5_009=retain power with no compromises.
ATOW_End5_010=inspire a successful rebellion.
ATOW_End5_011= And when the situation required persuasive tactics, they 
ATOW_End5_012=never faltered. Their outspoken fealty deftly retaining power for all these generations.
ATOW_End5_013=negotiated a peaceful transition without the need to destroy portions of the village.
ATOW_End5_014=used destructive tools to orchestrate a sabotage even when it hurt this fair village of {townname}.
ATOW_End5_015=Their suggestions pressed glory for the crown and crown alone, even when it inconvenienced the people.
ATOW_End5_016=Their suggestions pressed a positive agenda for the people of the realm. While demonstrably out of character, it allowed for an easy return to power.
ATOW_End5_017= Three generations of service, dedication, and influence.
ATOW_End5_018=My own continued story? Why, as of yet I haven't felt the same inclination to follow in my dear progenitors' footsteps. My service, as newly appointed royal advisor, {winner} IV, right-hand to the crown, leaves me dreadfully little time for hobbies. Maybe someday I shall lift a pipette; it is so difficult to know the future.
ATOW_End5_019=I now have a passion of a different sort and this competitive chapter is complete. And not a moment too soon; it is time for tea.

# passages/00256-ATOW-End6.mws.yaml
ATOW_End6_001=Tipping the Scales
ATOW_End6_002=This is not a story of Icarian fate where rampant ambition overwhelms reason. No, it is a story of wartime oppression and dismissal by inbred monarchs who would blindly penalize neoteric enterprise instead of embracing the glory of modern advanced experimentation. 
ATOW_End6_003=This is a story of three full generations of dedicated service by a proud Hungarian family with a rich history who were then flippantly cast out of their homes to live in exile. And for what? For revealing an uncomfortable truth? For showing that true science has the power to shape worlds and equally crush them within its grasp? My parents **could not evade the royal scrutiny** and here I exist, expatriated, wrenched from the work bequeathed to me. 
ATOW_End6_004=Oh, how I wish I could view the well-kept estate of my youth with its comforting stone walls and ivy-laden iron gates. To gaze out of the northern veranda to the valley and watch the peasants wade through the smog like toads amongst the slough. 
ATOW_End6_005=But even as I, {winner}, have tasted the sweetness of victory, I cannot savor it. The war is over. The legacy is severed. Pity me, for I know not what path to trod. I only hope these words spark something within you, dear reader, that you may not share the same fate as I. 

# passages/00257-ATOW-End7.mws.yaml
ATOW_End7_001=History of Applied Sciences
ATOW_End7_002=The 11th Edition of this coursebook has been provided by the glorious nation of Hungary, sponsored by the {townname} region, as a required companion to the Applied Sciences curriculum. It has been recently revised under the guidance of the author, Dr. {winner}.
ATOW_End7_003=_Instructors:_ Once reading has been completed, offer appropriate time for discussion. Individually, students should then answer the questions below.
ATOW_End7_004=**REVIEW QUESTIONS**
ATOW_End7_005=**1.** Who is **{winner}**?
ATOW_End7_006=**2.** In what year was **{newmeat}**
ATOW_End7_007=introduced? How did {newmeat}
ATOW_End7_008=affect the great war effort?
ATOW_End7_009=**3.** {winner} was born on the outskirts of {townname}. What is the name of the famous outpost that supplied the civil war efforts in the 1890's?
ATOW_End7_010=**4.** What was the critical importance of the **{_rnd_ATOW_End7_0}**? Illustrate.
ATOW_End7_011=**5.** What nation is the greatest and **only** nation in the world?

# passages/00258-ATOW-End8.mws.yaml
ATOW_End8_001=Local Legend
ATOW_End8_002=I submit this post-script as the fourth generation to take on the {winner} name. The printing costs have already mounted to a sum which I find difficult to manage after the **collapse of the war effort** and the subsequent reparation policies levied against this country to weaken its ability to muster new troops. 
ATOW_End8_003=With the inability for leaders to **make the difficult and needed decisions** to press the war effort forward, the conflict was lost even before it began. 
ATOW_End8_004=While practical in theory, I recognize that the processing of enemy soldiers into consumable goods was an unfortunate practice that potentially renders this work unreadable to some.
ATOW_End8_005=I can only hope those lost in the tragic biochemical release will find some solace in the revelation herein of the true source of the attack.
ATOW_End8_006=I am aware of what my lineage represents to the international community, and while I wish to distance myself from the whole affair, I also could not in good conscience allow the manuscripts I unearthed be destroyed. With its release, I hope to show - in all its graphic detail - that not all intentions were negative and that the science still holds true even to this day.
ATOW_End8_007=With righteous conviction and humility in my heart, I am forever your servant. - Dr. {winner}

# passages/00259-NoteENDings.mws.yaml
NoteENDings_001={winner} wrote Memoir in most cases.
NoteENDings_002=Ending 4
NoteENDings_003=Ending 3

# passages/00260-ATOW-Preparations.mws.yaml
ATOW_Preparations_001=Preparations
ATOW_Preparations_002=Complete the standard setup for {playtxt} players as shown in the rulebook. _Note that the_ {icon:angrymob_icon} _Track and starting player will be set by the Storybook in the coming pages._
ATOW_Preparations_003=Then, retrieve the **A Time of War** Scenario box, which will contain all components needed for this story. As the Storybook progresses, it will ask you to put items into play from this box. Be sure to keep it nearby.

# passages/00262-2PBlameGameEvent.mws.yaml
_2PBlameGameEvent_001=The Dilemma
_2PBlameGameEvent_002=My cousin and I were about to be faced with a pivotal decision when a group of loyal soldiers arrived at our doorstep. In the previous months we had made a simple pact to keep the knowledge of our activities secret. But alliances are particularly tenuous when multiple timelines overlap. 
_2PBlameGameEvent_003=Could I trust my own flesh and blood to honor our agreement?
_2PBlameGameEvent_004=**Rules**
_2PBlameGameEvent_005=If both players _remain silent_, they will each **gain 2 Resources** _(Knowledge or Ingredients)_ **of their choice at the start of the next Generation.**
_2PBlameGameEvent_006=If both players _accuse_ one another of traitorous activity, they both must **discard 2 Resources** of any type from their Estate or **return a Servant to Lost**.
_2PBlameGameEvent_007=If one player accuses and the other remains silent, the player who remains silent must **immediately discard one Estate Upgrade from their Estate and gains 2** {icon:creepy_icon}**.** _If they do not have an Estate Upgrade built, they must instead lose 5VP._

# passages/00263-CoWEventb.mws.yaml
CoWEventb_002=A **YAY** vote is a vote to rule with **benevolence**. It will reward choices that aid the people or move the {icon:s3_crowntoken} to the LEFT.
CoWEventb_003=A **NAY** vote is a vote to rule with an **iron fist**. It will reward greedy choices that hurt the people or decrees that move the {icon:s3_crowntoken} to the RIGHT.
CoWEventb_004=This will provide a **{decbon}VP** bonus at the End of the Generation to the player(s) who has made the most decrees that **helped** or **hurt** the people. **This includes decrees that have already been made.**
CoWEventb_005=_A tied vote will result in_ **benevolence** _being chosen._

# passages/00264-2PCoWEvent.mws.yaml
_2PCoWEvent_003=Once both players are ready, reveal the amount of money bid simultaneously. The winning player will gain **4VP** and the right to choose whether to rule with **benevolence** or with an **iron fist**.
_2PCoWEvent_004=**Benevolence** will reward choices that aid the people or move the {icon:s3_crowntoken} to the right.
_2PCoWEvent_005=**Iron Fist** will reward greedy choices that hurt the people or move the {icon:s3_crowntoken} to the left.
_2PCoWEvent_006=This will provide a **{decbon}VP** bonus at the End of the Generation to the player(s) who has made the most decrees that **helped** or **hurt** the people. 
_2PCoWEvent_007=_A tied vote will result in no player winning the bid and_ **benevolence** _being chosen._
_2PCoWEvent_009=Click to complete the bid...

# passages/00265-2PCoWRes.mws.yaml
_2PCoWRes_001=Bid Result
_2PCoWRes_002=The player who bid the most coins pays them to the supply and **gains 4VP.**
_2PCoWRes_003=They then make the following choice. _(If there is a tie, no money is paid, the outcome chosen must be_ **benevolence**_, and no player receives the bonus VP)_.
_2PCoWRes_004=**The winner of the bid chooses an option below:**
_2PCoWRes_005=We chose to rule with benevolence.
_2PCoWRes_006=We chose to rule with an iron fist.

