# passages/00298-Paradox3b.mws.yaml
Paradox3b_001=**Angry Mob Return**
Paradox3b_002=All {icon:angrymob_icon} icons are in effect once again. As normal, if a player meets or exceeds the Angry Mob token on the Creepy Track, they cannot perform actions in Town. 
Paradox3b_003={icon:storybooktoken}**University**
Paradox3b_004=With the near-total destruction of {townname}, there is no one available to honor scientific achievement. **This will no longer be awarded**.

# passages/00299-Reign1.mws.yaml
Reign1_002=Decision
Reign1_003=Dilemma
Reign1_004=Conundrum
Reign1_005=**Royal {_rnd_Reign1_0}**
Reign1_006=After a brief dinner,
Reign1_007=With some rejuvenating spirits and food in our bellies,
Reign1_008=I easily ingratiated myself into the man's inner circle with a gentle financial nudge. Soon,
Reign1_009={_rnd_Reign1_1} the royal advisor confided in me that he felt somewhat stifled by what he deemed "insignificant matters of this region." I, of course, offered to aide in his endeavors.
Reign1_010=It was only proper that my assistance would result in a boon for my own ventures. In fact, the precise decision I made had very little effect on the region itself insomuch that I cannot recall what it was. The most important question was, would benevolence or cruelty serve me best?
Reign1_011=I took the side of the people.
Reign1_012= This will result in: {crownL} {ch1}
Reign1_013=To hell with the people.
Reign1_014= This will result in: {crownR} {ch2}

# passages/00300-Reign1b.mws.yaml
Reign1b_002=waxing his mustache.
Reign1b_003=adjusting his girdle.
Reign1b_004=sampling wine and cheese.
Reign1b_005=The advisor thanked me for the assistance. From our short conversation, I knew that my friend was quite put upon by decision-making processes. I was quite certain that he would do as I suggested as contemplation would only waste time that could be better spent {_rnd_Reign1b_0}

# passages/00301-Reign2.mws.yaml
Reign2_001=**Drifters**
Reign2_002=The royal advisor seemed wracked with indecision over the recent plague of homelessness in the region. It had come to his attention that a dreadful crowd of shifty-eyed drifters had recently arrived in the township and were panhandling near the farmer's market. To think that some individuals choose to live a nomadic lifestyle!
Reign2_003=**It was of my most humble opinion that we should:**
Reign2_004=Offer the scamps temporary lodging.
Reign2_005=_This will result in:{crownL} All players may pay $1 to gain a **body** ingredient._
Reign2_006=Run the rabble off.

# passages/00302-Reign4.mws.yaml
Reign4_001=**Freedom of Speech**
Reign4_002=Civil war and the bloodshed it caused seemed to have not settled the hearts and minds of many of the citizens in the region. Across the valley, echoes of small protests over minor issues such as famine, over-taxing, and the proliferation of disease became commonplace.
Reign4_003=The advisor was tasked with quelling the mob, but was woefully unequipped mentally and physically to enforce such a choice. As a person strong of heart and steeped in personal liberty, I took it upon myself to offer advice. I would decide whether these Separatists idealists would escape or face further persecution.
Reign4_005=Allow Demonstrations. 
Reign4_006=_This will result in:{crownL} The negative effect for having a Separatist token will be removed._
Reign4_007=Crack Down.
Reign4_008=_This will result in:{crownR} A player with a Separatist token face-up cannot place their Self into Town at all._

# passages/00303-Reign3.mws.yaml
Reign3_001=**The Hunting Grounds**
Reign3_002=It was with a heavy heart that the royal advisor informed me that the royalty wanted to expand their hunting grounds to encompass part of the region. This was to both ensure good numbers for sport, but also to discourage poaching which had apparently run rampant.
Reign3_003=Allowing general hunting would carry with it a price, however it would make the people happy. But was it worth it to meddle in the affairs of nobles, especially with such rewards on the line?
Reign3_004=Allow Hunting.
Reign3_005=_This will result in:{crownL}Choose one **animal token** and return it to the game box. This animal can be in the possession of another player._
Reign3_006=Disallow Hunting.

# passages/00304-Reign6.mws.yaml
Reign6_001=**Spiritualism Craze**
Reign6_002=A fad of spirit rappings is spreading across the region and the royalty is being pressed by a regional temperance movement to outlaw this profane sport of seance. The advisor could not recall what a spirit rapping, a seance, or even note a time when he had witnessed a spiritualism meeting in the area, and the thought furrowed his brow severely. 
Reign6_003=Being well-versed in simple arcane practices - a fact I did not relay to my well-fed companion - I offered my assistance in the matter. General summoning of the spirits of the dead would provide cover for some of my family's peculiar traits, but perhaps I could provide a heretic for the royals to dislike.
Reign6_004=**The choice was obvious to me:**
Reign6_005=Allow the people their fun.
Reign6_006=_This will result in:{crownL}All players **lose 2{icon:creepy_icon}.** You gain 2VP._
Reign6_007=This is sacrilege!
Reign6_008=_This will result in:{crownR} Choose a player to immediately **gain 2{icon:creepy_icon}**._

# passages/00305-Reign7.mws.yaml
Reign7_001=**The Choice of Recognition**
Reign7_002=As fortune would have it, my esteemed companion, the royal advisor had quickly imbibed the majority of bottle of absinthe and promptly passed out upon the floor amongst his own evening's meal. Still lain fresh upon the dinner table was a contract with a royal seal.
Reign7_003=Now, I would not stoop to signing banker's cheques that were not my own, but considering the paper did require advisement as to whom should receive said goods or title, I was intrigued by the possibility and took up the authority. I could sign my name to the document, thereby granting myself any title or I could procure a little extra business in the region. It would be somewhat selfish to simply take the title, but it was alluring nonetheless.
Reign7_004=A little for myself.
Reign7_005=_This will result in:{crownL} {ch1}_
Reign7_006=Glory to ME.
Reign7_007=_This will result in:{crownR} Choose your own title that will display with your name for the rest of the story._

# passages/00306-Reign8.mws.yaml
Reign8_001=**Weapon Technology**
Reign8_002=The war had taken its toll upon the landscape and as time began to mend the rift between the general populace and the royalty, the subject of Advanced Weaponry (spearheaded by our illustrious family) and if it would be available to the common folk became a new topic of conversation. A topic that my dear royal advisor was pressed upon to make decisive action.
Reign8_003=The question had little significance to me. I would find a way to benefit from their continued use and improvement either way.
Reign8_004=**The choice was obvious to me. I chose:**
Reign8_005=Legalize their sale.
Reign8_006=_This will result in:{crownL}Gain 1 Weapon token. Weapon tokens can be spent as money. $1 per Weapon token._
Reign8_007=Restrict their sale.
Reign8_008=_This will result in:{crownR}Gain 1 Weapon token. Weapon tokens are worth 1VP at Game End._

# passages/00307-Reign3b.mws.yaml
Reign3b_002=The advisor thanked me for the assistance. I was happy to have control over such a strained situation. 
Reign3b_003=As expected, open season resulted in the extinction of one of our great native species. Survival of the fittest, I suppose.
Reign3b_004={crownL} Choose one **animal token** and return it to the game box. This animal can be in the possession of another player.

# passages/00308-Reign4b.mws.yaml
Reign4b_001=The advisor thanked me for the assistance. The situation was under control. 
Reign4b_002=Personal freedom, as always, was paramount to me.
Reign4b_003=There will be no mercy for traitors. The military would see to their dispersal.
Reign4b_004={crownR} Any player with a Separatist token face-up will no longer be able to place their Self into town.
Reign4b_005={crownL} The negative effect for having a Separatist token will be removed. The restriction on Self tokens is lifted. 

# passages/00309-Reign6b.mws.yaml
Reign6b_001=Thank You
Reign6b_002=The advisor thanked me for the assistance. Religion is such a delicate matter. 
Reign6b_003=And by treating it without any delicacy whatsoever, my cousins and I enjoyed a moments respite from general persecution.
Reign6b_004=It could not be taken lightly. My cousin would do well to remember this next time!
Reign6b_005={crownR} Choose a player to immediately **gain 2** {icon:creepy_icon}.
Reign6b_006={crownL} All players **lose 2** {icon:creepy_icon}**.**You gain 2VP.

# passages/00310-Reign8b.mws.yaml
Reign8b_001=The advisor thanked me for the assistance. Money or fame was always such a difficult choice. 
Reign8b_002=But, in this case, it was hard to resist the additional funds to fuel my schemes.
Reign8b_003=In the end, however, I could not waste such a precious resource on mere peasants. The pen may be mightier than the sword, but not mightier than a Helmet-Mounted Flamethrower.
Reign8b_004={crownR} Gain 1 {icon:s3_weapontoken} token. Weapon tokens are now worth **1VP** each at Game End.
Reign8b_006={crownL}Gain 1 {icon:s3_weapontoken} token. {icon:s3_weapontoken} tokens can now be spent as money. $1 per {icon:s3_weapontoken} token.

# passages/00311-Reign2b.mws.yaml
Reign2b_001=A Note of Thanks
Reign2b_002=The advisor thanked me for the assistance. I was quite obliged by the compliment, but our mutually beneficial arrangement suited my needs splendidly. 
Reign2b_003=The drifters would certainly be put to work, I'm sure.
Reign2b_004=It was unfortunately not the season to house visitors, even if they were meant to be temporary.
Reign2b_005={crownL} Then, all players may pay $1 to gain a **body** ingredient.

